window.CASE_DATA = {"source":"Clinical casebook — naturopathic case studies with protocols, chapters 1–5","caveat":"These are transcribed case records: what was presented and what was prescribed for that patient, kept as the casebook writes them. They are not treatment recommendations, they carry no clinical authority, and several use doses, routes or botanicals that would not be chosen today. Where a case carries a real hazard — a teratogenic dose, a cardiac glycoside, a low-dose botanical, an interaction, or a presentation that is an emergency — a safety note says so; those notes were written for this tool and are not in the source.","chapters":["Addictions","Cardiovascular Medicine","Dermatology","Endocrinology","Gastroenterology"],"cases":[{"id":"case1","n":1,"chapter":"Addictions","title":"In Utero Multi-Substance Addiction","condition":"Neonatal abstinence syndrome","presentation":"Infant exposed in utero to methadone, cocaine, heroin, tobacco and alcohol; presented with midbrain upregulation, feeding aggression and hyperactivity, and chronic diarrhea.","sections":[{"name":"Nutritional & neurochemical protocol","items":[{"agent":"Glycine","dose":"250 mg QD","why":"To calm the midbrain."},{"agent":"GABA","dose":"100 mg BID","why":"To quiet and centre midbrain tone."}]},{"name":"Homeopathic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Croton tiglium 6X","dose":"2 tablets BID","why":"Targeted to arrest chronic diarrhea."}]},{"name":"Clinical considerations","text":"Aggressive prenatal intervention and continuous postpartum monitoring are essential to prevent parental relapse and neurodevelopmental impairment."}],"patient":"9-month-old infant"},{"id":"case2","n":2,"chapter":"Addictions","title":"Opiate & Heroin Addiction","condition":"Opioid use disorder","presentation":"Prescribed Vicodin after a motor vehicle accident, progressing to high-dose OxyContin, Percocet and intravenous black tar heroin.","sections":[{"name":"Primary botanical protocol","items":[{"agent":"Lactuca virosa (wild lettuce) 1:1 fluid extract","dose":"90 drops every 3 hours"}]},{"name":"Sleep & neurochemical support","items":[{"agent":"Passiflora incarnata (passionflower) with Valeriana officinalis (valerian)"},{"agent":"GABA and glycine","dose":"At night"}]},{"name":"Clinical notes & alternatives","items":[{"agent":"Lactuca quercina decoction","dose":"1 tsp cut and sifted herb per cup of water, decocted, every 2–4 hours","why":"Acts as an alternative to morphine for severe chronic pain and opiate weaning."},{"agent":"Avena sativa (green oat) capsules or tea","dose":"Up to 2 capsules 4–6 times daily"}]}],"patient":"Adult","caution":"Lactuca virosa and L. quercina are sedative and, at the doses given here, are being used as an opioid substitute in withdrawal — a setting where autonomic instability, dehydration and relapse risk need medical supervision rather than self-management."},{"id":"case3","n":3,"chapter":"Addictions","title":"Alcoholism Rehabilitation & Liver Support","condition":"Alcohol use disorder","presentation":"History of chronic alcohol and cannabis use, current tobacco use (half a pack a day), fatigue, paraspinal spasm, hip pain, dysmenorrhea, and reactive hypoglycemia with a fasting blood glucose of 64 mg/dL.","sections":[{"name":"Nutritional & botanical protocol","items":[{"agent":"Glycobalance","why":"Multivitamin rich in B-complex and balanced minerals."},{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"200 mcg QD","why":"Hepatic detoxification support."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"Daily","why":"Adrenal support and catecholamine synthesis."},{"agent":"Tryptophan","dose":"Evening dose","why":"Elevates serotonin and promotes sleep."},{"agent":"Magnesium (“43 Plus”)","dose":"200 mg BID","why":"Uterine smooth muscle relaxation."},{"agent":"Essential fatty acids","why":"Omega-3 and omega-6 to replace damaged dietary fats."},{"agent":"Lobelia inflata tincture","dose":"5 drops in a cup of water, 3–6 times daily PRN","why":"To curb nicotine cravings."}]},{"name":"Dietary strategy","text":"Small, frequent protein and complex-carbohydrate meals to stabilise blood sugar in the 80–100 mg/dL target range."},{"name":"Physical medicine protocol","items":[{"agent":"Detoxification massage","dose":"Weekly","why":"Supine right-sided myofascial stretching, releasing right-sided guarding from liver inflammation."},{"agent":"Liver meridian tracing","why":"Manual tracing from medial foot to groin, dispersing excess liver fire."},{"agent":"Castor oil packs","dose":"30 minutes with a hot water bottle","why":"Placed over the hepatic region."},{"agent":"Thoracic spinal manipulation","dose":"T7–T10","why":"Relieves autonomic tension to liver, gallbladder, stomach and pancreas."},{"agent":"Reflexology","why":"Pancreatic and hepatic foot zones at the instep midpoint."}]},{"name":"Acute alcoholism protocols","items":[{"agent":"Panthenol with taurine","dose":"Panthenol 300 mg QD and taurine 3000 mg QD","why":"Stimulates aldehyde dehydrogenase to clear acetaldehyde toxicity."}]}],"patient":"35-year-old female, 1 year sober"},{"id":"case4","n":4,"chapter":"Addictions","title":"Cocaine Detoxification","condition":"Stimulant use disorder","presentation":"Six months sober following a 15-year poly-substance history; presenting with multi-joint inflammatory arthralgia (knees, shoulders, elbows, MCPs) and elevated liver transaminases.","sections":[{"name":"Anti-inflammatory & joint support","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Bromelain / curcumin","dose":"1000 mg BID","why":"Joint inflammation."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"2000 mg BID"}]},{"name":"Hepatic & energy protocol","items":[{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"200 mcg QD"},{"agent":"Cola nitida (kola nut) powder","dose":"¼ tsp dissolved in liquid several times daily","why":"A flavonoid-rich coffee substitute stimulant."},{"agent":"Immugen","why":"Immune system formula support."},{"agent":"Strict alcohol-free formulations","why":"All tinctures and extracts formulated in non-alcoholic media."},{"agent":"Hydration","dose":"A minimum of 3 additional large glasses of pure water daily"}]},{"name":"Alternative considerations","items":[{"agent":"SAMe, GABA and glycine","why":"Mood support."},{"agent":"Avena sativa","dose":"2 capsules 4–5 times daily"}]}],"patient":"44-year-old male"},{"id":"case5","n":5,"chapter":"Addictions","title":"Heroin (Diacetylmorphine) Withdrawal","condition":"Opioid use disorder","presentation":"Severe black tar heroin dependency with concurrent cannabis and amphetamine use.","sections":[{"name":"Phytotherapy & neurotransmitter regimen","items":[{"agent":"Lactuca quercina (wild lettuce)","dose":"1 tsp dried herb infused in 1 cup boiling water TID","why":"Suppresses midbrain locus coeruleus agitation and eases muscular pain."},{"agent":"Glycine","dose":"1 tsp powder TID"},{"agent":"GABA","dose":"1000 mg TID"},{"agent":"Botanical sedative compound","dose":"60 drops QID","why":"Equal parts Eschscholzia californica, Passiflora incarnata, Scutellaria lateriflora and Valeriana officinalis."},{"agent":"Vitamin B1 (thiamine)","dose":"100 mg BID"},{"agent":"Broad-spectrum multivitamin and multimineral","dose":"1 QD"}]},{"name":"Adjunctive therapies","text":"Frequent cervical and thoracic adjustments; strict blood sugar maintenance."},{"name":"Alternative acute opiate withdrawal formulas (Dr Alan Gaby IV protocol)","items":[{"agent":"Intravenous infusion","dose":"Repeated twice across 7 days","why":"3.5 g vitamin C, 5 mL 20% magnesium chloride hexahydrate, 2.5 mL 10% calcium gluconate, 1000 mcg vitamin B12, 100 mg pyridoxine, 250 mg dexpanthenol and 1 mL vitamin B-complex 100."},{"agent":"High-dose EPA and DHA","dose":"EPA 2250 mg and DHA 500 mg","why":"To modulate aggression, anger and impulsivity."}]}],"patient":"23-year-old male","caution":"Thiamine before glucose in anyone with a history of alcohol or poly-substance use — a glucose load given first can precipitate Wernicke encephalopathy. The intravenous protocol is a physician-administered procedure."},{"id":"case6","n":6,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Angina Pectoris","condition":"Angina pectoris","presentation":"Daily chest pain, severe multijoint arthritis, pseudogout, and hypercholesterolemia (total cholesterol 235–265 mg/dL) while on atorvastatin (Lipitor 20 mg QD).","sections":[{"name":"Core cardiovascular protocol","items":[{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp BID","why":"Red grape, elderberry, blueberry, aronia berry, red raspberry and pomegranate — arrests LDL oxidation and preserves endothelial elasticity."},{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"300 mcg QD"},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. (hawthorn) berry solid extract","dose":"½ tsp QD","why":"Standardised to procyanidin B2."},{"agent":"Thorne “SAT”","dose":"3 capsules BID","why":"Siliphos (milk thistle), artichoke and curcumin for hepatic clearance."}]},{"name":"Dietary exclusions","text":"Complete avoidance of margarine, trans fats, commercial ice cream, chips, dips, deep-fried foods and heavy dairy creams."},{"name":"Acute angina relievers","items":[{"agent":"Cactus grandiflorus (night-blooming cereus)","dose":"10 drops every 30 minutes up to 4 doses, then 10 drops BID maintenance"},{"agent":"Terminalia arjuna","dose":"500 mg TID"},{"agent":"Glonoine 3X homeopathic","dose":"3 sublingual pellets every 15 minutes until relief"},{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"400 mg QD continuously for a minimum of 1 year"}]}],"patient":"57-year-old male","caution":"Chest pain that is new, changed in pattern, or not relieved by rest is unstable angina or infarction until proven otherwise, and none of these agents substitute for that assessment."},{"id":"case7","n":7,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Sinus Arrhythmia & Stress-Induced Irregular Heartbeat","condition":"Cardiac arrhythmia","presentation":"Irregular heart rhythm exacerbated by poor diet, high occupational stress and heavy beer consumption; GGTP elevated to 130 U/L.","sections":[{"name":"Therapeutic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Magnesium / potassium aspartate","dose":"2 capsules TID for a larger body habitus; the standard dose is 2 capsules BID","why":"80 mg magnesium and 80 mg potassium per capsule."}]},{"name":"Diet & lifestyle","text":"Heavy alcohol intake reduction, increased pure water, and fresh salads."},{"name":"Physical medicine","text":"Weekly acupuncture, chiropractic adjustments, and foot reflexology."}],"patient":"50-year-old male"},{"id":"case8","n":8,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Arrhythmia & Fibrocystic Breast Disease","condition":"Cardiac arrhythmia","presentation":"Palpitations and irregular pulse accompanied by bilateral, dense fibrocystic breast masses.","sections":[{"name":"Arrhythmia protocol","items":[{"agent":"Potassium citrate","dose":"2 capsules QD"},{"agent":"Potassium magnesium aspartate","dose":"2 capsules QPM","why":"Delivers 200 mg elemental potassium and magnesium daily."},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"2 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Vitamin B6","dose":"50 mg QD"},{"agent":"Vitamin A","dose":"1 capsule QD"}]},{"name":"Dietary prescription","text":"High-potassium foods (kelp, sunflower seeds, almonds, yams, chard, spinach, raisins) and anti-arrhythmic omega-3 sources; strict avoidance of coffee, black tea, colas and chocolate."},{"name":"Cystic breast adjunct","items":[{"agent":"Lugol's iodine","why":"Applied to a cotton tampon and placed against the cervix (Dr Jonathan Wright method)."}]}],"patient":"43-year-old female","also":["Fibrocystic breast changes"],"caution":"The intravaginal Lugol's application is transcribed as the case records it. Iodine is absorbed readily across vaginal mucosa, can provoke mucosal burns, and can disturb thyroid function — it is not a self-administered therapy, and is contraindicated in pregnancy and in thyroid disease."},{"id":"case9","n":9,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Adrenergic Intercostal Myalgia & Stress-Induced Chest Pain","condition":"Non-cardiac chest pain","presentation":"Recurrent, stress-induced non-cardiac chest pain; normotensive on atenolol; borderline lipid elevation.","sections":[{"name":"Cardiovascular regimen","items":[{"agent":"CoQ10","dose":"100 mg QD"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"2 tsp BID"},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry solid extract","dose":"½ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Calcium / magnesium","dose":"300 mg / 100 mg, 1 QD"},{"agent":"Thorne “Neo-Cardio”","dose":"1 capsule BID","why":"Niacin, magnesium, Terminalia arjuna, Inula racemosa, Ammi visnaga, Astragalus membranaceus and bromelain."},{"agent":"Broad-spectrum multivitamin and mineral with liver detox support"}]}],"patient":"35-year-old male"},{"id":"case10","n":10,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Post-Bypass Secondary Prevention & Peripheral Hypoperfusion","condition":"Atherosclerosis","presentation":"After a six-way coronary artery bypass graft, presenting with chronically cold hands while taking dipyridamole, enteric aspirin and acetaminophen.","sections":[{"name":"Antioxidant & microvascular regimen","items":[{"agent":"Niasafe 600 (inositol hexaniacinate)","dose":"600 mg QD"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp QD in water"},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid","dose":"500 mg QD"},{"agent":"Crataegus berry / Rosa canina (rose hips) 50/50 solid extract","dose":"1 tsp QD"},{"agent":"Lecithin","dose":"1 heaping tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Green tea","dose":"Daily infusion"}]},{"name":"Lipid antioxidant synergistic complex","items":[{"agent":"Full-spectrum vitamin E (alpha, beta, gamma, delta tocopherols)","dose":"800 IU QD"},{"agent":"Mixed tocotrienols (alpha, beta, gamma, delta)","dose":"60 mg QD with meals"},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg QD"},{"agent":"CoQ10","dose":"100 mg QD"}]},{"name":"Laxative counter-measure","items":[{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"500 mg QD","why":"Added to prevent constipation from the extracts."}]}],"patient":"66-year-old male","caution":"Vitamin E at 800 IU alongside aspirin and dipyridamole compounds antiplatelet effect; bleeding risk and any planned procedure need to be weighed by the prescribing physician."},{"id":"case11","n":11,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Simple Hypercholesterolemia","condition":"Hyperlipidemia","presentation":"Total cholesterol 252 mg/dL, LDL 174 mg/dL, overweight at 185 lbs.","sections":[{"name":"Therapeutic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Pantethine (Cholestame)","dose":"200 mg BID; standard therapeutic titration up to 300 mg TID"},{"agent":"Polymethoxylated flavonoids and tocotrienol complex","dose":"300 mg QD"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"CoQ10","dose":"60 mg QD"},{"agent":"Cod liver oil","dose":"3 capsules QD"},{"agent":"Alpha lipoic acid","dose":"200 mg QD"},{"agent":"Lecithin","dose":"300 mg QD"},{"agent":"Lutein","dose":"10 mg QD"}]},{"name":"Diet","text":"Caloric reduction to 2200 kcal/day; absolute removal of hydrogenated and trans fats."}],"patient":"47-year-old female"},{"id":"case12","n":12,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Familial Hypercholesterolemia with Retinopathy","condition":"Hyperlipidemia","presentation":"Stubborn cholesterol (275–315 mg/dL), triglycerides 214 mg/dL, LDL 186 mg/dL, blood pressure 135/95 mmHg, and myopic retinal degeneration.","sections":[{"name":"Combined lipid & retinal protocol","items":[{"agent":"Policosanol compound (LaSante Cholesterol Support)","dose":"10 mg policosanol","why":"Combined with guggulsterones, garlic extract and vitamin E."},{"agent":"Pantethine","dose":"300 mg TID"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"High dose","why":"Retinal microcirculation and LDL protection."},{"agent":"I-Comp","why":"Ocular antioxidant formula."},{"agent":"CoQ10","dose":"30 mg QD"},{"agent":"Alpha lipoic acid","dose":"1 capsule QD"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1 capsule BID"}]},{"name":"Dietary protocol","text":"Transition to wild-caught fish (salmon, cod); elimination of all margarine, commercial ice creams, cream-based soups and trans fats; replacement with cold-pressed olive and flaxseed oils."}],"patient":"59-year-old male"},{"id":"case13","n":13,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Type IV Endogenous Hyperglyceridemia","condition":"Hyperlipidemia","presentation":"Triglycerides 970 mg/dL, total cholesterol 269 mg/dL, severe postprandial somnolence, peripheral paresthesias and nocturnal diaphoresis.","sections":[{"name":"Endogenous hyperglyceridemia protocol","items":[{"agent":"Red yeast rice extract","dose":"1200 mg BID"},{"agent":"Pantethine","dose":"300 mg TID"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp BID"},{"agent":"Soluble dietary fibre","dose":"Marked increase","why":"Retards intestinal fat absorption."}]},{"name":"Dietary shift","text":"Elimination of fried foods, buttermilk and refined sugars; substitution with fresh fruits and steamed cruciferous vegetables."}],"patient":"64-year-old female","caution":"Red yeast rice contains monacolin K, which is lovastatin — the same myopathy, hepatotoxicity and interaction profile applies, and it must not be stacked on a prescribed statin. Triglycerides near 1000 mg/dL carry a real risk of acute pancreatitis."},{"id":"case14","n":14,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Severe Hyperlipidemia Post-Lymphoma","condition":"Hyperlipidemia","presentation":"Post-splenectomy, a Stage IA lymphocytic lymphoma survivor with refractory hyperlipidemia: cholesterol 401 mg/dL, triglycerides 554 mg/dL, and an incalculable LDL above 300 mg/dL.","sections":[{"name":"Dietary macro-structure","items":[{"agent":"Breakfast","why":"Steel-cut oatmeal infused with fresh blueberries, non-fat organic milk, and strong green tea."},{"agent":"Lunch","why":"Wild-caught cold-water fish rich in EPA and DHA (no farmed fish) with raw salad and clear broths."},{"agent":"Dinner","why":"Yams, sweet potatoes, winter squash, steamed green vegetables, brown rice, and 2 oz of lean clean protein."},{"agent":"Between-meal and evening snacks","why":"Fresh or frozen wild blueberries."},{"agent":"Eliminations","why":"Pastries, cheeses, cured meats and hydrogenated oils."}]}],"patient":"60-year-old female"},{"id":"case15","n":15,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Familial Combined Hyperlipidemia (Type IIb Fredrickson Phenotype)","condition":"Hyperlipidemia","presentation":"Severe hereditary Apo B-100 overproduction; total cholesterol 310 mg/dL, triglycerides 325 mg/dL, HDL 35 mg/dL; a failed treadmill stress test and multi-vessel coronary artery disease on angiogram.","sections":[{"name":"Progressive titration protocol","items":[{"agent":"Niacin (nicotinic acid) titration","dose":"Week 1: 50 mg TID. Week 2: 100 mg TID. Gradually advance to 1000 mg TID, titrated up to 3000 mg daily","why":"Taken strictly with meals to diminish prostaglandin flushing, under routine liver function and uric acid monitoring."},{"agent":"Omega-3 fatty acids (flaxseed oil)","dose":"1 tsp QD","why":"Blocks hepatic VLDL assembly."},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. solid extract","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"2 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Red yeast rice extract","dose":"600 mg BID"},{"agent":"Garlic","dose":"Daily","why":"Anti-platelet and anti-thrombotic."}]},{"name":"Diet & exercise","text":"Caloric restriction from 3900 to 2500 kcal/day; strict fat intake under 30 g daily; 45 minutes of resistance work three times weekly plus two one-hour aerobic walks."},{"name":"Integrative co-management","text":"Successfully paired with low-dose lovastatin (20 mg) and gemfibrozil (120 mg) where lifestyle compliance was incomplete."}],"caution":"Red yeast rice is lovastatin by another name; pairing it with prescribed lovastatin, as the co-management note describes, doubles the statin dose. Niacin at gram doses raises uric acid and glucose and can precipitate gout and hepatotoxicity."},{"id":"case16","n":16,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Mild Essential Hypertension","condition":"Hypertension","presentation":"Blood pressure 162/94 mmHg, visceral weight gain, and high occupational stress.","sections":[{"name":"Antihypertensive protocol","items":[{"agent":"Botanical formula","dose":"10 drops BID","why":"1 part Rauvolfia serpentina (1:5 tincture) and 1 part Tilia europaea (linden flower, 1:5 tincture)."},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry and plant solid extract","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"200 mg BID"}]},{"name":"Dietary regimen","text":"A 500 kcal daily caloric deficit; strict elimination of canned soups and heavily salted prepared foods; 1 cup of water every 2 hours."}],"patient":"47-year-old male","caution":"Rauvolfia contains reserpine, which depletes central catecholamines: it can precipitate severe depression and suicidality, and is contraindicated with a history of depression or peptic ulcer."},{"id":"case17","n":17,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Severe Hypertension with Manganese Deficiency","condition":"Hypertension","presentation":"Refractory hypertension at 190/100 mmHg, severe fatigue, flatulence, ocular allergies and ovarian neuralgia; hair mineral analysis demonstrated severe manganese depletion (0.01 ppm against a normal 0.10–1.0).","sections":[{"name":"Trace mineral & neuro-vascular protocol","items":[{"agent":"Manganese glycerophosphate","dose":"1 capsule daily at lunch","why":"Normalised blood pressure to 176/91 within 20 days and lowered cholesterol from 276 to 230 mg/dL."},{"agent":"Naringenin (grapefruit bioflavonoid)","dose":"Several capsules BID","why":"Inhibits 9-hydroxyprostaglandin dehydrogenase, preserving prostacyclin PGI2 while blunting vasoconstrictive 6-keto-PGE1 and the renal renin cascade."},{"agent":"Ovarian neuralgia tincture","dose":"30 drops BID","why":"Equal parts Cimicifuga racemosa, Piscidia erythrina and Cypripedium calceolus."},{"agent":"Adjuncts","why":"L-lysine for ocular viral inflammation, thymotrophin glandular protomorphogen, choline 1 QD, and Causticum 30X homeopathic for chronic palpebral inflammation."}]}],"patient":"62-year-old female","caution":"Naringenin is the grapefruit constituent that inhibits intestinal CYP3A4 — it raises blood levels of many drugs, calcium channel blockers and statins among them. Cypripedium is a conservation-listed genus."},{"id":"case18","n":18,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Hypertension & Natural Diuresis","condition":"Hypertension","presentation":"Hypertension at 180/100 mmHg refractory to Dyazide; diverticulosis, dry skin and allergic rhinitis.","sections":[{"name":"Alternative diuretic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Vitamin B6 (pyridoxine)","dose":"Therapeutic daily dosing","why":"Acts as a physiologic diuretic."},{"agent":"Botanical diuretic compound","dose":"60 drops TID","why":"1 part Usnea spp., 1 part Petroselinum crispum (parsley) and 1 part Sambucus nigra (elder) flower."},{"agent":"Magnesium","why":"To relax colonic hypertonicity."},{"agent":"Lycopodium 200X homeopathic","dose":"Single constitutional dose"}]}],"patient":"65-year-old female"},{"id":"case19","n":19,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Hypotension & Orthostatic Dysautonomia","condition":"Hypotension and orthostatic intolerance","presentation":"Blood pressure 90/60 mmHg, chronic palpitations, cold extremities, diaphragm spasm, pre-syncopal “white outs”, and chronic constipation from severe hyponatremia.","sections":[{"name":"Fluid volume & digestive protocol","items":[{"agent":"Dietary sodium expansion","why":"Unrestricted liberal sea-salting of all whole foods."},{"agent":"Magnesium and potassium aspartate","dose":"160 mg of each BID"},{"agent":"Bitter digestive tonic","dose":"10 drops after meals","why":"1 part Gentiana lutea, 1 part Berberis aquifolium, 1 part Artemisia annua — stimulates gastric HCl, promotes peristalsis and aids mineral chelation."}]}],"patient":"42-year-old female"},{"id":"case20","n":20,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Post-Surgical Mitral Stenosis Arrhythmia","condition":"Cardiac arrhythmia","presentation":"A 10-year history of chronic arrhythmia following mitral valve commissurotomy, with concurrent breast cancer radiation recovery.","sections":[{"name":"Arrhythmia resolution protocol","items":[{"agent":"Magnesium and potassium aspartate","dose":"2 capsules BID, titrated to 2 capsules TID for recalcitrant arrhythmias","why":"Providing 160 mg elemental magnesium and 160 mg potassium BID."},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp QD in water"},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry extract","dose":"½ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"1 tsp QD"}]},{"name":"Oncology recovery support","items":[{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"150 mcg QD"},{"agent":"Zinc","dose":"100 mg QD"},{"agent":"Beta-carotene drops","dose":"150,000 IU QD"},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"6 g daily"}]}],"patient":"Adult female","caution":"Zinc at 100 mg daily induces copper deficiency within months; it needs paired copper and a defined end point."},{"id":"case21","n":21,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Post-Coronary Bypass Congestive Decompensation & Dyspnea","condition":"Congestive heart failure","presentation":"A history of three-way bypass, current tobacco use, chest tightness, exertional dyspnea, polycythemic hemoconcentration (haematocrit 51.5%) and dyslipidemia.","sections":[{"name":"Cardiovascular recovery regimen","items":[{"agent":"Convallaria majalis (lily of the valley) tincture","dose":"5 drops BID","why":"An inotropic cardiotonic acting like the digitalis glycosides."},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry solid extract","dose":"½ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Cardio-Guard Plus with CoQ10","dose":"2 capsules QD"},{"agent":"Ginkgo biloba extract","why":"Platelet-activating factor inhibitor, lowering shear blood viscosity."},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"2 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Vitamin E","dose":"1000 IU QD"},{"agent":"Therapeutic rehydration","why":"Forced water intake to decrease the elevated haematocrit."}]}],"patient":"67-year-old male","caution":"Convallaria is a cardiac glycoside herb with a narrow therapeutic index and the same toxicity and interaction profile as digoxin; it is on the low-dose botanical list for that reason."},{"id":"case22","n":22,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Post-Stroke Cerebrovascular Rehabilitation","condition":"Stroke and cerebrovascular rehabilitation","presentation":"Chronic residual hemiparesis, cognitive impairment and vascular instability secondary to an oral contraceptive-induced thromboembolic stroke at age 22.","sections":[{"name":"Cerebrovascular & fibrinolytic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Cerebral microcirculation tincture","dose":"60 drops BID","why":"Equal parts Zingiber officinale, Ginkgo biloba and Ruscus aculeatus."},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"2 tbsp BID"},{"agent":"Nattokinase","dose":"Daily","why":"Breaks down intravascular fibrin matrices and clears arterial debris."},{"agent":"Bromelain / curcumin","dose":"Between meals","why":"Systemic proteolytic anti-inflammatory."},{"agent":"Phosphatidylcholine / lecithin","dose":"High daily dosing","why":"Restores damaged neuronal and glial membranes."},{"agent":"Vitamin E","dose":"600 IU QD"}]}],"patient":"Adult female","caution":"Nattokinase, ginkgo, bromelain and vitamin E are each antithrombotic; stacked, and especially alongside prescribed anticoagulation, they raise haemorrhagic risk in a patient who has already had a cerebrovascular event."},{"id":"case23","n":23,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Chronic Post-Traumatic Thrombophlebitis","condition":"Thrombophlebitis","presentation":"Pain, induration and venous insufficiency along the left greater saphenous vein, consequent to a childhood femur fracture.","sections":[{"name":"Venous & lymphatic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Thorne “Venocap”","dose":"1 capsule TID","why":"Centella asiatica, Aesculus hippocastanum, diosmin, Hamamelis virginiana, grape seed OPCs and Ruscus aculeatus."},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"1–2 tbsp QD","why":"Reduces platelet stickiness."},{"agent":"Dietary carotenes and anthocyanins","dose":"A minimum of 1 cup of fresh dark berries daily","why":"Fortifies venous basement membranes."},{"agent":"Topical Hamamelis virginiana (witch hazel)","why":"Cold liquid compresses applied with soaked toweling."},{"agent":"Postural drainage","why":"Nocturnal elevation of the lower extremity above the level of the right atrium."}]},{"name":"Alternative venous strengthening botanical","items":[{"agent":"Galium aparine (cleavers) fluid extract","dose":"60 drops TID for 6 continuous months"}]}],"patient":"33-year-old female"},{"id":"case24","n":24,"chapter":"Cardiovascular Medicine","title":"Severe Varicosities & Systemic Lymphatic Stasis","condition":"Varicose veins","presentation":"Massive calf varicosities, generalised doughy and boggy lymphadenopathy, post-insect-bite flu-like episodes, and seasonal affective depression.","sections":[{"name":"Lymphatic pumping & venotonic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Phytolacca decandra (poke root) tincture","dose":"15 drops BID"},{"agent":"Aesculus hippocastanum and Ruscus aculeatus","why":"Venous wall elasticity and lymphatic return."},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry extract","why":"Vascular muscular tone and myocardial performance."},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid","dose":"500 mg QD","why":"Adrenal endurance."},{"agent":"L-tyrosine","why":"Dopaminergic energy stimulation and winter lethargy."},{"agent":"Postural lymphatic drainage exercises","why":"Lying supine with the buttocks flush to the wall and legs extended vertically at 90 degrees, paired with rhythmic thoracic and spinal back rolls."}]}],"patient":"39-year-old male","caution":"Phytolacca is a low-dose botanical — it is emetic and purgative above small doses and the root is the most toxic part."},{"id":"case25","n":25,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Acne Vulgaris","condition":"Acne","presentation":"Diffuse, highly inflammatory facial and upper back comedones, pustules and sebaceous overactivity.","sections":[{"name":"Hepatobiliary steroid clearance regimen","items":[{"agent":"Zinc","dose":"50–100 mg QD, raised to 100 mg BID for the first 2–3 weeks","why":"Balanced with 2–4 mg elemental copper in a multimineral base."},{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"400 mcg QD for 2 weeks, then 200 mcg QD maintenance"},{"agent":"Vitamin B6","dose":"50 mg QD–BID","why":"Especially effective where the acne is hormonally driven."},{"agent":"High-dose fat-soluble therapy","dose":"Vitamin A 100,000 IU QD with vitamin E 800 IU QD","why":"Under periodic hepatic enzyme monitoring."},{"agent":"Vitamin D","dose":"1000 IU BID"},{"agent":"Berberis aquifolium fluid extract","dose":"60 drops BID"}]},{"name":"Systemic acne botanical compound","items":[{"agent":"Compound tincture","dose":"60 drops BID","why":"1 part each Vitex agnus-castus, Berberis aquifolium, Arctium lappa root and Urtica dioica whole plant."}]},{"name":"Topical interventions","items":[{"agent":"Calendula officinalis warm wraps","why":"60 drops of tincture in a bowl of warm water, applied as a compress to draw purulence and disinfect follicles."},{"agent":"Topical 4% niacinamide cream or 20% azelaic acid cream"}]},{"name":"Physical medicine","text":"Reflexology to the large intestine, spleen, gallbladder and liver zones; gentle thoracic spinal manipulation at T7–T12; alternating facial hydrotherapy (1 minute hot, 30 seconds cold, 4 cycles)."}],"patient":"16-year-old male","caution":"Vitamin A at 100,000 IU daily is above the tolerable upper intake and is teratogenic. It must not be given to anyone who could become pregnant without contraception, and the hepatic monitoring the case specifies is not optional."},{"id":"case26","n":26,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Adolescent Female Acne","condition":"Acne","presentation":"Widespread facial comedones exacerbated by an ultra-low-protein vegan diet.","sections":[{"name":"Prescription","items":[{"agent":"Zinc","dose":"60 mg QD"},{"agent":"Bromelain and curcumin","dose":"1500 mg with meals","why":"Digestive proteolysis."},{"agent":"Hepatobiliary formula","dose":"15 drops per meal","why":"Equal parts Berberis aquifolium, Chelidonium majus and Chionanthus virginicus."}]}],"patient":"17-year-old vegan","caution":"Chelidonium majus is a documented cause of idiosyncratic hepatitis; it warrants liver enzyme monitoring and immediate withdrawal if transaminases rise."},{"id":"case27","n":27,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Infantile “Baby Acne” & Secondary Urticaria","condition":"Acne","presentation":"Papular eruptions from maternal breast milk estrogens, later evolving into saliva-reactive facial hives.","sections":[{"name":"Maternal protocol","text":"Complete avoidance of fried, hydrogenated foods and simple sweets; flaxseed oil 1 tsp QD; selenium 200 mcg QD to assist maternal steroid clearance."},{"name":"Infant protocol","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"⅛ tsp daily in water or breast milk"},{"agent":"Urtica urens 12X homeopathic","dose":"2 sublingual pellets melted daily"},{"agent":"Infant maintenance","why":"Zinc 5 mg QD, vitamin K1 oil 1–2 drops QD, and a liquid pediatric multimineral."}]}],"patient":"1-month-old infant","also":["Urticaria and angioedema"]},{"id":"case28","n":28,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Recurrent Cutaneous Furunculosis (Boils)","condition":"Folliculitis and boils","presentation":"Recurrent, deep-seated staphylococcal furuncles.","sections":[{"name":"Traditional decoctive therapy","items":[{"agent":"Wild alder bush bark (Alnus spp.)","dose":"Two quart canning jars boiled in water, strained, and consumed in divided doses across 2 days"},{"agent":"Boiled yellow onion broth with raw honey","dose":"Taken concurrently"},{"agent":"Arctium lappa (burdock) root","why":"Incorporated for alterative action."},{"agent":"Staphylococcus 12X homeopathic"}]}]},{"id":"case29","n":29,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Recurrent Streptococcal / Staphylococcal Cellulitis","condition":"Cellulitis","presentation":"Fiery red, edematous, intensely painful lower extremity cellulitis with inguinal lymphadenopathy and lymphatic stasis.","sections":[{"name":"Acute flares protocol","items":[{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp QD","why":"Natural microvascular support."},{"agent":"Aesculus hippocastanum and Ruscus aculeatus extract","dose":"60 drops BID"},{"agent":"Rhus toxicodendron 12X to 200X homeopathic","dose":"3 pellets melted sublingually QD","why":"Specifically indicated where leg pain is improved by continuous motion."},{"agent":"Staphylococcus 12X homeopathic","why":"Intermittent nosode support."}]},{"name":"Integrative escalation threshold","text":"Ibuprofen 200 mg TID for 3 days at the early prodrome, followed by cephalexin 250 mg QID for 10 days if suppuration or lymphangitis advances."}],"patient":"55-year-old male","caution":"Spreading cellulitis with fever, lymphangitic streaking or systemic upset is a same-day medical problem; the escalation threshold in this case is the point at which botanical management stops."},{"id":"case30","n":30,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Pyridoxine-Induced Histaminic Dermatitis","condition":"Drug eruptions","presentation":"Confluent, macular, non-papular pruritic erythema triggered by long-term high-dose vitamin B6 (200 mg daily for 2 years) under heavy stress.","sections":[{"name":"De-escalation & clearance protocol","items":[{"agent":"Immediate cessation","why":"Absolute removal of all supplemental vitamin B6."},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp TID","why":"Histamine suppression."},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra solid extract","dose":"¼ tsp QD","why":"Adrenal cortisol modulation."},{"agent":"Bile salts","dose":"2 tablets with major meals","why":"Facilitates lipid-soluble processing."},{"agent":"Hepatoprotection","why":"A compound of Silybum marianum, Cynara (artichoke) and Curcuma longa."}]}],"caution":"Long-term pyridoxine above roughly 100 mg daily also causes a sensory peripheral neuropathy, which is the more serious consequence of the same exposure and is only partly reversible."},{"id":"case31","n":31,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"“Fragile” Hyper-Reactive Eczematous Dermatitis","condition":"Eczema","presentation":"Exudative, highly sensitive dermatitis on the forearms and hands, triggered rapidly by trans fats, fried carbohydrates and the premenstrual phase.","sections":[{"name":"Eczema protocol","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"2 tsp QD","why":"Alters phospholipid membrane fatty acid pools."},{"agent":"Dietary singlet oxygen quenchers","why":"High dietary beta-carotene — yams, carrots, dark leafy greens."},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra solid extract","dose":"¼ tsp QAM","why":"Blocks leukotrienes B4 and D4 through licochalcone action and spares endogenous cortisol."},{"agent":"Tri-Quench (potassium iodide)","dose":"5 drops QD","why":"Quenches triplet-sensitised reactive molecules."},{"agent":"Juglans nigra / cinerea (walnut / butternut) tincture","dose":"20 drops BID"},{"agent":"Comprehensive digestive enzymes","dose":"2 capsules per meal"},{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"200 mcg QD"},{"agent":"Sulphur 200X homeopathic","dose":"Constitutional single dose"}]}],"patient":"24-year-old female","caution":"Glycyrrhiza at solid-extract doses raises blood pressure and depletes potassium through pseudoaldosteronism; it is the one agent here that needs a blood pressure check on review."},{"id":"case32","n":32,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Erysipelas (“St Anthony's Fire”)","condition":"Cellulitis","presentation":"Blazing red, painful facial erythema, fever to 101°F, cephalalgia, nausea and burning cutaneous plaques from Streptococcus pyogenes.","sections":[{"name":"Botanical & homeopathic regimen","items":[{"agent":"Streptococcus 12X homeopathic","dose":"3 pellets BID"},{"agent":"Systemic antibacterial extract","dose":"45 drops TID","why":"Equal parts Gentiana lutea and Berberis aquifolium."},{"agent":"Adrenal cortisol / endurance formula","dose":"60 drops BID","why":"Equal parts Eleutherococcus senticosus and Glycyrrhiza glabra."},{"agent":"Hydrastis canadensis (goldenseal) root powder","dose":"500 mg orally every 3 hours"}]},{"name":"Critical medical caution","text":"Erysipelas can progress rapidly; standard pharmacological intervention — penicillin V 500 mg BID for 10 days, erythromycin 250 mg every 6 hours, or a cephalosporin — must be initiated immediately if bacteremia threatens."}],"patient":"48-year-old female"},{"id":"case33","n":33,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Post-Shaving Folliculitis with Concurrent Migraines","condition":"Folliculitis and boils","presentation":"Suppurative, pustular hair follicle inflammation across the anterior neck, with chronic migraines every other day.","sections":[{"name":"Protocol","items":[{"agent":"Dietary elimination","why":"Complete removal of all dairy and aged cheeses, eliminating the dietary tyramines driving the cephalalgia."},{"agent":"Staphylococcus 12X homeopathic","dose":"3 pellets twice weekly"},{"agent":"Zinc","dose":"90 mg QD for 30 days, then tapered to 60 mg QD"},{"agent":"Folliculitis botanical compound","dose":"30 drops BID","why":"Berberis aquifolium and Baptisia tinctoria (wild indigo) with concentrated liquid zinc, vitamin B12 and folic acid drops built directly into the dropper bottle."},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate and cod liver oil","why":"Microvascular support."}]}],"patient":"14-year-old male","also":["Migraine"]},{"id":"case34","n":34,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Recurrent Oral Herpes Simplex (HSV-1)","condition":"Herpes simplex","presentation":"Relapsing labial cold sores with systemic hypocholesterolemia (total cholesterol 110 mg/dL, LDL 47 mg/dL) and compromised cellular immunity.","sections":[{"name":"Antiviral & epithelial protocol","items":[{"agent":"L-lysine","dose":"2000 mg QD","why":"Competitively antagonises viral arginine uptake."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1500 mg BID"},{"agent":"Cod liver oil","dose":"3 pearls QD","why":"Repairs the mucosal basement membrane."},{"agent":"Dietary cholesterol repletion","why":"Whole pasture-raised eggs added daily to support steroid and cell-membrane synthesis."},{"agent":"Topical antiviral","dose":"Applied locally up to 6 times daily during outbreaks","why":"Licrogel (pure glycyrrhetinic acid from licorice root) or Melissa officinalis (lemon balm) gel."},{"agent":"Astragalus membranaceus tincture","dose":"30 drops BID","why":"Immune maintenance."}]}],"patient":"39-year-old male"},{"id":"case35","n":35,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Herpes Zoster (Shingles)","condition":"Herpes zoster","presentation":"Unilateral, dermatomal vesicular eruption with intense neuralgic stinging across the mid-back.","sections":[{"name":"Acute neuro-immune regimen","items":[{"agent":"Vitamin B12 (cyanocobalamin or hydroxocobalamin) injection","dose":"1 mL IM or subcutaneous every other day","why":"Paired with folic acid to prevent post-herpetic neuralgia."},{"agent":"Zinc","dose":"50 mg BID"},{"agent":"Cod liver oil","dose":"3 pearls QD"},{"agent":"Echinacea / Hydrastis immune formula","dose":"3 capsules BID–TID"},{"agent":"Rhus toxicodendron 200X homeopathic","dose":"5 sublingual pellets at bedtime","why":"Until the herpetic vesicles crust and dry completely."},{"agent":"Herpeszostin homeopathic drops","dose":"5 drops TID"}]}],"patient":"33-year-old male","caution":"Antiviral therapy started within 72 hours of the rash is what reduces post-herpetic neuralgia; zoster involving the ophthalmic division, the ear, or a disseminated rash is an urgent referral."},{"id":"case36","n":36,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Incontinentia Pigmenti (Bloch-Sulzberger Syndrome)","condition":"Incontinentia pigmenti","presentation":"Hyperpigmented, linear, verrucous hyperkeratotic skin lesions with severe intrinsic asthma and failure to thrive.","sections":[{"name":"Supportive epithelial regimen","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp BID","why":"Mast-cell stabilisation for the asthma."},{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"100 mcg QD","why":"Supports glutathione peroxidase in liver and skin."},{"agent":"Carotenoids","dose":"High-dose dietary and supplemental","why":"Soothes chronic cutaneous micro-inflammation."},{"agent":"Vitamin E and vitamin C","dose":"Nutritional dosing","why":"Cellular membrane protection."},{"agent":"Dietary overhaul","why":"Total removal of hot dogs, cured sausages, margarine, commercial ice cream and packaged bakery goods."}]}],"patient":"3-year-old female","also":["Asthma"]},{"id":"case37","n":37,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Lomatium dissectum Exanthematous Drug Rash","condition":"Drug eruptions","presentation":"Sudden-onset, confluent, full-body morbilliform macular exanthem appearing 24 hours after ingesting Lomatium dissectum tincture for viral respiratory symptoms.","sections":[{"name":"Detoxification protocol","items":[{"agent":"Immediate cessation","why":"Immediate discontinuation of all Lomatium-containing botanicals."},{"agent":"Forced hydration","dose":"High volume","why":"To clear circulating diterpenes."},{"agent":"Botanical liver & lymph flush","dose":"60 drops BID","why":"1 part Peumus boldus (boldo), 1 part Chelidonium majus (greater celandine), 1 part Ceanothus americanus (red root), and 0.1 part Podophyllum peltatum (mayapple — 1 fluid dram added into a 2 oz compound bottle)."},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra tea and slippery elm lozenges","why":"For residual throat irritation."}]}],"patient":"35-year-old female","caution":"The whole-body rash Lomatium is known for is the reason for the protocol; adding Podophyllum, a cytotoxic purgative, and Chelidonium, a hepatotoxin, to clear a drug reaction carries its own risk and belongs under supervision."},{"id":"case38","n":38,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Multiple Subcutaneous Lipomas","condition":"Lipoma","presentation":"Progressive development of multiple subcutaneous lipomas across bilateral forearms and thighs; severe hypertriglyceridemia at 325 mg/dL, total cholesterol 204 mg/dL, and low HDL at 26 mg/dL.","sections":[{"name":"Lipid clearance protocol","items":[{"agent":"Lipotropic factor complex","dose":"2 capsules TID"},{"agent":"Vitamin E","dose":"400 IU QD"},{"agent":"Balanced multimineral","dose":"2 capsules BID"},{"agent":"Dietary protocol","why":"Complete elimination of all trans fats, margarine, cheeses, peanut products, whole wheat and refined sugars; structured around pigmented root vegetables, cruciferous greens, non-citrus fruits, wild rice, millet and lean poultry and fish."}]}],"patient":"37-year-old male","outcome":"A 30 lb weight loss, triglycerides down to 85 mg/dL, and a slight reduction in lipoma diameter."},{"id":"case39","n":39,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Molluscum Contagiosum","condition":"Molluscum contagiosum","presentation":"Two pediatric presentations: a 4-year-old boy with seven discrete lesions, and a 5-year-old girl with widespread popliteal clusters.","sections":[{"name":"Case A — 4-year-old boy, seven discrete lesions","items":[{"agent":"Internal regimen","why":"Vitamin C 500 mg QD, cod liver oil, pantothenic acid 200 mg QD, and an oral liquid vitamin A and zinc compound — 1 capful on Monday, Wednesday and Friday."},{"agent":"Topical alternation","why":"Glycyrrhizic acid liquid or gel in the morning; Melaleuca alternifolia (tea tree) ointment locally at bedtime."}]},{"name":"Case B — 5-year-old girl, widespread popliteal clusters","items":[{"agent":"Internal regimen","why":"Cod liver oil, elemental zinc 20 mg, quercetin powder, vitamin C 150 mg QD."},{"agent":"Topical keratolytic / antiviral protocol","dose":"Daily","why":"Lightly score the surface of the largest lesions with fine-grit sandpaper to break the waxy capsule, then immediately paint with a topical solution of Melissa officinalis and Podophyllum peltatum tincture."}]}],"patient":"Pediatric","caution":"Podophyllum resin is cytotoxic and systemically absorbed through broken skin — the scoring step is exactly what raises that absorption. It is contraindicated in pregnancy, and molluscum is self-limiting in children, which is the argument against aggressive treatment at all."},{"id":"case40","n":40,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Morphea (Localised / Linear Scleroderma)","condition":"Morphea","presentation":"Linear patches of indurated, collagenous, violaceous scleroderma on the arms and face, threatening “en coup de sabre” hemifacial atrophy.","sections":[{"name":"Antioxidant & collagen modulating protocol","items":[{"agent":"Vitamin E","dose":"400 IU BID","why":"Critical to inhibit excessive fibrogenesis."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg QD"},{"agent":"Cod liver oil","dose":"2 tsp QD","why":"Supplies high-potency vitamin A and omega-3 fatty acids."},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"2 tsp QD"},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp TID"},{"agent":"Rosa canina and Crataegus spp. solid extract","dose":"½ tsp of each QD"},{"agent":"Systemic candida clearance (Can-Pro)","why":"Anti-candida packet."},{"agent":"Diet","why":"Very high carotenoid intake — dark greens, orange squashes, carrots — green tea, and elimination of damaged and fried fats."}]}],"patient":"37-year-old female"},{"id":"case41","n":41,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA)","condition":"MRSA skin infection","presentation":"A deep decubitus ulcer on the sacrum and an infected catheter site with antibiotic-resistant MRSA, in a hospitalised, terminal patient.","sections":[{"name":"High-potency antimicrobial regimen","items":[{"agent":"Oral / systemic botanical tincture","dose":"60 drops QID","why":"5 parts Hydrastis canadensis, 5 parts Baptisia tinctoria, 1 part Lomatium dissectum isolate. In severe refractory presentations, powdered Hydrastis and Baptisia can be escalated to four “00” capsules QID, up to 6 times daily."},{"agent":"Topical antimicrobial salve","dose":"Applied generously directly to the decubitus crater","why":"Vag-Pac base (gynecologic drawing paste) reinforced with Calendula officinalis and Stellaria media (chickweed) extracts."}]}],"patient":"74-year-old female","caution":"MRSA in a hospitalised patient with a deep pressure ulcer is a culture-and-sensitivity problem with real bacteremia risk; this was adjunctive care in a terminal patient, not an alternative to antimicrobial therapy."},{"id":"case42","n":42,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Pilonidal Cyst","condition":"Pilonidal cyst","presentation":"Recurrent, suppurative sacrococcygeal pilonidal abscess with concomitant pubic folliculitis and back acne.","sections":[{"name":"Surgical & drawing protocol","items":[{"agent":"Procedural intervention","why":"Surgical lancing, purulent expression, thorough irrigation, and closure with sterile butterfly tape."},{"agent":"Topical drawing poultice","why":"A compound salve of Stellaria media (chickweed) and Hydrastis canadensis root powder, or Vag-Pac paste applied as an osmotic drawing pack."},{"agent":"Staphylococcus 12X homeopathic","why":"Constitutional folliculitis coverage."},{"agent":"Allantoin gel from Symphytum officinale (comfrey)","why":"Applied topically for epithelial rebuilding, with oral zinc and increased pure water."}]}],"patient":"29-year-old female","also":["Folliculitis and boils"],"caution":"Comfrey allantoin closes the surface fast, which is the wrong thing over an undrained cavity — sealing a pilonidal sinus before the tract is clear is how it recurs. Comfrey is also hepatotoxic taken internally."},{"id":"case43","n":43,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Plantar Verrucae (Plantar Warts)","condition":"Warts","presentation":"Five approaches recorded for plantar verrucae.","sections":[{"name":"Protocol 1 — Podophyllum & occlusion","text":"Paint the verruca nightly with Podophyllum peltatum tincture; cover during daylight hours with impermeable adhesive tape. In the evening, peel the tape back — stripping devitalised superficial hyperkeratotic layers — and re-apply Podophyllum."},{"name":"Protocol 2 — Fresh garlic & pantothenate","text":"Slice a raw Allium sativum clove to the precise diameter of the wart and tape it securely over the lesion overnight. Remove in the morning, wear plain adhesive tape all day, and repeat for 6 consecutive cycles. Pair with oral pantothenic acid 500 mg QD to warm cold extremities."},{"name":"Protocol 3 — Mentholatum","text":"Thick application of commercial mentholated vapour rub to the plantar lesions morning and evening for 2–3 weeks."},{"name":"Protocol 4 — Salicylic abrasion","text":"Debride the wart surface gently with fine sandpaper, then apply concentrated aspirin (acetylsalicylic acid) solution several times daily."},{"name":"Protocol 5 — Thalassotherapy","text":"Immune enhancement, stress reduction, and daily barefoot immersion in natural ocean saltwater and beach sand."}],"caution":"Podophyllum is cytotoxic, is absorbed through abraded skin, and is contraindicated in pregnancy. None of these debridement approaches belongs on the foot of a diabetic or anyone with peripheral neuropathy or arterial disease."},{"id":"case44","n":44,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Poison Ivy / Poison Oak Contact Dermatitis","condition":"Contact dermatitis","presentation":"Severe vesicular, intensely pruritic erythematous contact dermatitis from Toxicodendron radicans.","sections":[{"name":"Traditional Ojibwa jewelweed (Impatiens capensis / biflora) protocol","items":[{"agent":"Harvesting & extraction","why":"Crush fresh aerial stems and foliage in a sealed plastic bag and suspend it in hot sunlight to collect the running sap in the bag corner. Stabilise the juice by adding ½ oz vodka per pint of expressed liquid."},{"agent":"Topical application","why":"Apply the stabilised jewelweed liquid topically, or macerate 6 fresh leaves and stems directly over the blisters as a wet poultice for 2 hours."},{"agent":"Internal infusion","why":"Drink hot tea prepared by steeping 6 fresh jewelweed leaves in water."},{"agent":"Cryotherapy alternative","why":"Pre-freeze freshly harvested jewelweed tea into ice cubes and rub the ice directly over active flare-ups."}]}]},{"id":"case45","n":45,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Psoriasis","condition":"Psoriasis","presentation":"Three protocols: extensive plaque psoriasis in a 50-year-old male commercial fisherman; scalp and peripheral psoriasis in a 34-year-old female; and chronic scalp, aural and genital psoriasis in a 37-year-old female.","sections":[{"name":"Protocol A — nutritional & enzymatic foundation","items":[{"agent":"Omega-3 fatty acids","why":"Shifts arachidonic acid cascades; total ban on fried foods, trans fats, beer and carbonated beverages."},{"agent":"Bile salts","dose":"2 tablets with every main meal","why":"Facilitates gut fat assimilation and clearing of circulating enterotoxins."},{"agent":"Digestive enzymes","dose":"Pancreatin / Zypan 2–3 tablets per meal","why":"With Lactobacillus acidophilus, 1 AM and 2 PM."},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp TID, or 3 capsules AM and 2 capsules PM"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins","dose":"1 tbsp daily"},{"agent":"Silybum marianum with Berberis aquifolium","dose":"30 drops with meals"},{"agent":"Robert's Formula","dose":"2 capsules BID"}]},{"name":"Protocol A — intracellular signalling modulation","items":[{"agent":"Momordica charantia (bitter melon) 1:5 extract","dose":"90–120 drops BID","why":"Inhibits elevated guanylate cyclase activity, arresting runaway epidermal hyper-proliferation."},{"agent":"Ziziphus jujuba (red date)","dose":"10 dried fruits daily","why":"Elevates depressed intracellular cAMP."},{"agent":"Coleus forskohlii","why":"Herbal adenylate cyclase activator."}]},{"name":"Protocol A — high-dose vitamin D therapy","items":[{"agent":"Vitamin D3","dose":"5000 IU daily for month 1, tapering to 1000–2000 IU daily maintenance","why":"Plus daily natural sunlight exposure."}]},{"name":"Protocol A — Mitchell topical psoriasis cream","items":[{"agent":"Compounded cream","dose":"Applied nightly","why":"Equal parts tea tree ointment, Sting Stop (homeopathic), chickweed ointment, zinc oxide ointment, vitamin E oil and 1% hydrocortisone cream, incorporating topical vitamin D."}]},{"name":"Protocol B — scalp and peripheral psoriasis (34-year-old female)","text":"Vitamin D 1000 IU QD; Momordica charantia extract; selenium 250 mcg QD; Crataegus solid extract ½ tsp QD; topical Glycyrrhiza glabra gel; elimination of peanut butter, cheeses, oranges and commercial pizza."},{"name":"Protocol C — chronic scalp, aural and genital psoriasis (37-year-old female)","text":"Hepasil liver tonic 3 capsules BID; Glycyrrhiza glabra tincture; DGL powder ½ tsp BID; quercetin powder ¼ tsp TID; Momordica charantia 60 drops BID; glycine powder ½ tsp after dinner; dietary elimination of oranges and tangerines, removing the methoxy-flavonoids that tax liver pathways."}],"caution":"Momordica charantia is hypoglycaemic and abortifacient. Long-term daily hydrocortisone under occlusion thins skin and can rebound on withdrawal, and vitamin D at 5000 IU needs a 25-OH-D level rather than open-ended dosing."},{"id":"case46","n":46,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Post-Retin-A Cutaneous Reaction & Hormonal Edema","condition":"Drug eruptions","presentation":"Erythema, desquamation, facial swelling, unilateral numbness, diffuse alopecia, severe premenstrual fluid retention with a 7 lb gain, and severe constipation after tretinoin therapy.","sections":[{"name":"Rehabilitation regimen","items":[{"agent":"Immediate discontinuation","why":"Cease all Retin-A and topical tretinoin applications."},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra solid extract","dose":"¼ tsp QD","why":"Adrenal cortisol potentiation."},{"agent":"Hepatosplenic botanical compound","dose":"60 drops BID","why":"2 parts Cynara scolymus (artichoke), 1 part Angelica sinensis (dong quai), 3 parts Silybum marianum, later reinforced with 2 parts Mitchella repens."},{"agent":"Berberis aquifolium fluid extract","dose":"10 drops BID"},{"agent":"Zinc","dose":"50 mg BID","why":"Essential cofactor for DNA-dependent mRNA polymerase in hair and skin keratin synthesis."},{"agent":"Vitamin B6 (pyridoxine)","dose":"50 mg QD","why":"Premenstrual diuresis."},{"agent":"Dietary protein expansion","why":"Add whole farm eggs, supplying clean dietary cholesterol for steroidogenesis."}]}],"patient":"27-year-old female","also":["Alopecia"]},{"id":"case47","n":47,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Papulopustular Rosacea","condition":"Rosacea","presentation":"Prominent facial erythema, telangiectasias across the nose and cheeks (“malar mask”), inflammatory papulopustules, and constipation.","sections":[{"name":"Hypochlorhydria & digestive protocol","items":[{"agent":"Betaine HCl with digestive enzymes","dose":"Start at 5–10 grains per meal, titrating carefully up to 15–20 grains as tolerated"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID","why":"Blunts histamine and environmental reactive flushes."},{"agent":"N-acetyl-cysteine (NAC)","dose":"Daily","why":"Bonds and clears inflammatory dietary wheat lectins."},{"agent":"Dietary elimination","why":"Complete exclusion of specific IgG food allergens — cheese, corn, eggs, lima beans, dairy, mushrooms, soy, almonds, garlic — and fried potatoes."}]}],"patient":"43-year-old female","caution":"Betaine HCl is contraindicated with active peptic ulcer or on acid-suppressing therapy, and the titration is stopped by warmth or burning, not pushed through it."},{"id":"case48","n":48,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Chronic Seborrheic Dermatitis of the Scalp","condition":"Seborrheic dermatitis","presentation":"Severe scaling, pruritus and crusting along the anterior and posterior hairline, with irritable bowel syndrome and osteopenia.","sections":[{"name":"Fat-soluble vitamin synergy","items":[{"agent":"Cod liver oil","dose":"5 pearls daily","why":"Supplying 1250 IU of natural vitamin D."},{"agent":"Supplemental vitamin D3","dose":"An additional 400 IU daily","why":"Combined with direct scalp daylight exposure."},{"agent":"Vitamin K1","why":"Matures calcium-binding proteins and restores dry skin."},{"agent":"Vitamin E","dose":"400 IU QD"}]},{"name":"Topical antifungal scalp therapy","items":[{"agent":"Wise Woman Herbals tea tree ointment","dose":"Applied along the scalp margin nightly","why":"Never use undiluted pure essential tea tree oil directly on bare skin."}]},{"name":"Neuro-visceral IBS support","items":[{"agent":"Psyllium seed husks (Yerba Prima)","dose":"1 tsp QAM"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate"}]},{"name":"Urinary incontinence add-on","items":[{"agent":"Biotics Research “B-Vital”","dose":"2 capsules AM, 1 capsule PM","why":"750 mg Lepidium meyenii (maca root) and 50 mg velvet elk antler."}]}],"patient":"55-year-old female","also":["Irritable bowel syndrome"]},{"id":"case49","n":49,"chapter":"Dermatology","title":"Chronic Intractable Urticaria (Hives)","condition":"Urticaria and angioedema","presentation":"Four protocols: histamine and adrenal recovery in a 39-year-old female; vitamin K and homeopathic control in a 23-year-old female; chocolate hypersensitivity in a 35-year-old female; and cold-induced urticaria.","sections":[{"name":"Protocol 1 — histamine & adrenal recovery (39-year-old female)","items":[{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra solid extract","dose":"¼ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Tanacetum parthenium (feverfew) tincture","dose":"20 drops BID"},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg TID"},{"agent":"Dietary arachidonic acid suppression","why":"Eliminate chicken skin, dark chicken meat, ice cream, margarine, dairy fats, sausages, bacon, French fries, peanuts and peanut butter."}]},{"name":"Protocol 2 — vitamin K & homeopathic control (23-year-old female)","items":[{"agent":"Vitamin K1","dose":"20 mg QD, or heavily increased dark leafy greens","why":"Vitamin K biochemically completes and carboxylates calcium-handling proteins, stabilising the cell membrane calcium flux that drives dermal histamine degranulation."},{"agent":"Urtica urens 6X homeopathic","dose":"3 pellets BID"},{"agent":"Passiflora incarnata tea","dose":"Daily","why":"Nerve sedative."},{"agent":"Vitamin B-complex","dose":"High potency daily","why":"Stress support."}]},{"name":"Protocol 3 — chocolate hypersensitivity urticaria (35-year-old female)","text":"Magnesium supplementation, since deficiency exacerbates compulsive chocolate cravings; a multivitamin and mineral; restriction of cocoa products; and a shoe lift correcting a 1 cm anatomical short leg."},{"name":"Protocol 4 — cold-induced urticaria (“cold allergy”)","items":[{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"200 mg BID"},{"agent":"Vitamin K1","dose":"20 mg QD"},{"agent":"Urtica dioica 3X homeopathic, or freeze-dried Urtica dioica leaf capsules","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Protective winter thermal wear","why":"With elimination of chilled and cold dairy fats."}]}],"caution":"Vitamin K1 at 20 mg daily antagonises warfarin outright. Urticaria with any lip, tongue or throat swelling, or wheeze, is anaphylaxis and is treated as such."},{"id":"case50","n":50,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Adrenal Fatigue & Endocrine Adaptogen Protocol","condition":"Adrenal fatigue","presentation":"Severe legal stress, chronic constipation, paraspinal spasm and exhaustion.","sections":[{"name":"Adrenal adaptogenic formula","items":[{"agent":"Alfalfa (Medicago sativa) and licorice (Glycyrrhiza glabra) 50/50 solid extract","dose":"¼ tsp QD, or 2 capsules of each QD","why":"To spare endogenous cortisol."},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid (vitamin B5)","dose":"500 mg QD","why":"Essential precursor for coenzyme A in steroidogenesis."},{"agent":"Adrenal desiccated protomorphogen","dose":"3–4 capsules at lunchtime"},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"500 mg TID"},{"agent":"Vitamin B-complex","dose":"About 10 mg per individual B vitamin"},{"agent":"Vitamin K1","why":"Bone support and osteocalcin carboxylation."},{"agent":"Crataegus oxyacantha extract","dose":"½ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Foot contrast hydrotherapy","dose":"2 minutes hot, 1 minute cold, alternating 4 cycles in large stainless bowls","why":"In the early afternoon."}]},{"name":"Modern adaptogen additions","items":[{"agent":"Eleutherococcus senticosus","dose":"90 drops BID"},{"agent":"Rhodiola rosea"}]}],"patient":"45-year-old female","caution":"Licorice solid extract taken daily raises blood pressure and depletes potassium; “adrenal fatigue” is not a recognised diagnosis, and true adrenal insufficiency needs a cortisol measurement before it is treated as exhaustion."},{"id":"case51","n":51,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus with Diabetic Ketoacidosis","condition":"Diabetes mellitus, type 1","presentation":"Polydipsia, polyuria, nausea, Kussmaul hyperventilation, blood glucose 624 mg/dL, serum bicarbonate 16 mEq/L, blood pH 7.15, and urine 4+ for glucose and ketones.","sections":[{"name":"Emergency stabilisation protocol","items":[{"agent":"Immediate oral alkalinisation","dose":"1 tsp sodium bicarbonate dissolved in a full glass of water"},{"agent":"Immediate emergency endocrinologic referral","why":"Hospitalisation for split-dose regular and lente insulin therapy — 40 units total, the morning shot 30% short-acting and 70% intermediate-acting, with regular insulin half an hour before lunch and dinner."}]},{"name":"Long-term beta-cell & microvascular protection","items":[{"agent":"Chromium","dose":"400 mcg QD"},{"agent":"Camellia sinensis (green tea) polyphenols","dose":"3 cups of strong green tea daily","why":"Tea bags brewed twice to yield high epicatechins for pancreatic beta-cell protection."},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID","why":"Inhibits aldose reductase and polyol pathway accumulation of sorbitol and galactitol, preventing diabetic cataracts and peripheral neuropathy."},{"agent":"Dietary carotenes and flavonoids","why":"Prevents diabetic retinopathy and capillary basement membrane microangiopathy."}]}],"patient":"22-year-old female","caution":"Diabetic ketoacidosis is a medical emergency needing intravenous fluids, insulin and electrolyte correction. Oral bicarbonate does not treat it and delay is what kills — the referral is the treatment, and everything else here is for after the crisis."},{"id":"case52","n":52,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus with Angina & Neuropathy","condition":"Diabetes mellitus, type 2","presentation":"Refractory obesity at 235 lbs, HbA1c 6.8%, fasting glucose 110–180 mg/dL, unstable angina, hypertension at 185/85 mmHg, and lower extremity peripheral neuropathy.","sections":[{"name":"Glycemic & neuropathic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Oplopanax horridus (devil's club) root bark tea","dose":"Brew 2 tsp in 2 cups of water; drink ½ cup daily","why":"Stabilises blood sugar into the 100–120 mg/dL range."},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp BID mixed strictly into 12 oz of pure water","why":"Hypoglycemic and vascular protective."},{"agent":"Chromium","dose":"200 mcg QD"},{"agent":"Capsaicin topical cream","dose":"Applied over the feet and ankles","why":"For diabetic neuropathy."},{"agent":"Botanical diuretic tincture","dose":"90 drops BID","why":"Equal parts Usnea spp. and Petroselinum crispum."},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry extract","why":"A safe and effective adjunct for blood pressure and cardiac microcirculation alongside antihypertensives."}]}],"patient":"72-year-old female","also":["Angina pectoris"]},{"id":"case53","n":53,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Non-Insulin-Dependent Diabetes Mellitus","condition":"Diabetes mellitus, type 2","presentation":"Fasting blood sugar 145 mg/dL, 2-hour postprandial glucose 250 mg/dL, and sedentary obesity at 242 lbs.","sections":[{"name":"Comprehensive glycemic reversal protocol","items":[{"agent":"Gymnema sylvestre extract","dose":"400 mg daily, or 1:5 tincture 20 drops BID","why":"Stimulates beta-cell repair and blunts sugar taste receptors."},{"agent":"Chromium","dose":"200 mcg BID","why":"Potentiates glucose tolerance factor and thermogenesis."},{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"200 mg BID","why":"Decreases cellular insulin resistance and protects the myocardium."},{"agent":"Biotin","dose":"10 mg QD","why":"Stimulates glucokinase and reduces blood glucose."},{"agent":"Vitamin B6","dose":"50 mg QD","why":"Inhibits advanced glycation end-products."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"500 mg BID–TID","why":"Competes with glucose for cellular transport and arrests sorbitol formation."},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp QD sipped slowly through the day in a large bottle of water"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID","why":"Aldose reductase inhibitor preventing cataracts and microangiopathy."},{"agent":"Camellia sinensis (green tea)","why":"Sweetened exclusively with pure Stevia rebaudiana leaf drops."}]},{"name":"Diet & exercise","text":"Caloric reduction to 3000 kcal/day and titrating down; strict protein allocation based on ideal body weight (64 g protein/day); 1 mile of daily track walking."},{"name":"Physical medicine","text":"Naturopathic spinal manipulation from T5 to T12 — liver, pancreas, stomach and duodenal innervation."},{"name":"Adjunctive candidates","text":"Syzygium jambolana, Momordica charantia, taurine to arrest platelet hyper-aggregation, and niacin 100 mg QD."}],"patient":"58-year-old male"},{"id":"case54","n":54,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Adult-Onset Diabetes Evaluation","condition":"Diabetes mellitus, type 2","presentation":"Fasting glucose 322–324 mg/dL, cholesterol 323 mg/dL, triglycerides 362 mg/dL, GGT 134 U/L, and blood pressure 160/85 mmHg.","sections":[{"name":"Botanical glycemic regimen","items":[{"agent":"Complex antidiabetic compound","dose":"20 drops TID","why":"Equal parts Oplopanax horridus, Opuntia spp. (prickly pear cactus), Cichorium intybus (chicory) and Artemisia absinthium."},{"agent":"Syzygium jambolana (jambul) tincture","dose":"20–60 drops BID"},{"agent":"Crataegus berry solid extract","dose":"½ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Quercetin chalcone","dose":"3 capsules BID"},{"agent":"Chromium, biotin, selenium and zinc","dose":"Chromium 200 mcg QD, biotin 1 mg QD, selenium 200 mcg QD, zinc 30 mg QD"},{"agent":"Naringenin","dose":"¼ tsp TID","why":"For the secondary hypertension."},{"agent":"Pancreatic enzymes","dose":"2 tablets per meal"}]},{"name":"Dietary transition","text":"Steel-cut oats with oat bran for breakfast; cold-water fish, brown rice and steamed greens for dinner; a total ban on refined sweets and fried fats."}],"patient":"59-year-old female","outcome":"Weight reduction from 199 to 154 lbs and glucose down to 188 mg/dL.","caution":"Artemisia absinthium contains thujone and is a low-dose botanical, not a long-term daily herb."},{"id":"case55","n":55,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Reactive Hypoglycemia & Rebound Hyperglycemia","condition":"Hypoglycemia","presentation":"An exaggerated glucose curve on a 6-hour GTT: fasting 85, a half-hour spike to 172, dropping to 52 mg/dL at hour 3 with mood volatility and tachycardia.","sections":[{"name":"Glycemic stabilisation protocol","items":[{"agent":"Chromium","dose":"400 mcg QD at breakfast"},{"agent":"Balanced multimineral","dose":"At dinner","why":"To counterbalance the morning chromium."},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra solid extract","dose":"¼ tsp QD","why":"Supports the adrenals through hypoglycemic troughs."},{"agent":"Vitamin B-complex and vitamin C","why":"Nutritional adrenal fortification."},{"agent":"Dietary rule","why":"Absolute elimination of refined sugars; three balanced meals daily with protein-rich snacks such as cashew or almond butter."}]}],"patient":"41-year-old female"},{"id":"case56","n":56,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Hashimoto's Thyroiditis (Chronic Lymphocytic Thyroiditis)","condition":"Hashimoto's thyroiditis","presentation":"Goiter with 10% enlargement, anti-TPO (microsomal) antibodies elevated to 1.8 U/mL, and dyslipidemia with cholesterol 274 mg/dL and LDL 168 mg/dL.","sections":[{"name":"Autoimmune & anti-fibrotic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Bromelain","dose":"1000 mg TID","why":"Taken with meals for digestion and between meals to lyse progressive thyroid follicular fibrosis."},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp BID","why":"Suppresses thyroid autoantibodies and systemic inflammation."},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry solid extract","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Glycine powder","dose":"½ tsp BID","why":"Calmative."},{"agent":"Cynara scolymus (artichoke)","why":"Rich in cellular protective phenylpropanoids."},{"agent":"Diet","why":"High-carotene diet; avoidance of peanuts, chocolate, margarine and aged cheese."}]},{"name":"Thyroid toning botanical compound (Dr Andrea Sullivan formula)","items":[{"agent":"Compound tincture","dose":"1 tsp BID–TID","why":"2 parts Serenoa repens (saw palmetto), 1 part Fucus vesiculosus (bladderwrack), 1 part Turnera diffusa (damiana), 1 part Cynara scolymus, 1 part Nasturtium officinale (watercress)."}]},{"name":"Physical medicine","text":"Weekly cervical spinal adjustments; cold hydrotherapy compresses applied to the anterior neck nightly; foot reflexology to the thyroid zone at the base of the first metatarsal."}],"patient":"35-year-old female","caution":"Fucus is an iodine source, and iodine can worsen autoimmune thyroiditis and precipitate either hypo- or hyperthyroidism in Hashimoto's; thyroid function needs monitoring on this formula."},{"id":"case57","n":57,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Subclinical Hypoadrenia & Latent Immune Weakness","condition":"Adrenal fatigue","presentation":"Recurrent sinusitis, recurrent vaginitis, low-normal salivary cortisol, a weak kidney pulse, and fatigue.","sections":[{"name":"Immune-adrenal restoration formula","items":[{"agent":"Compound tincture","dose":"60–90 drops BID","why":"Equal parts Astragalus membranaceus, Echinacea angustifolia, Glycyrrhiza glabra and Mitchella repens."},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid","dose":"500 mg at lunch"},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"2000 mg at lunch"},{"agent":"Borage oil","dose":"2 capsules QD","why":"Supplies dihomo-gamma-linolenic acid (DGLA, 20:3n-6)."},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"1 tsp QD"}]}],"patient":"38-year-old female"},{"id":"case58","n":58,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Hypoglycemia with Chronic Adrenal Exhaustion","condition":"Hypoglycemia","presentation":"Fasting glucose 55 mg/dL, severe afternoon lethargy, palpitations, anxiety, panic and rage when meals are missed, and a history of HSV-2 and HPV.","sections":[{"name":"Nutritional & endocrine regimen","items":[{"agent":"Dietary re-timing","why":"Strict consumption of a protein and fat breakfast; an absolute rule against fasting or skipping meals."},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid","dose":"250 mg QD"},{"agent":"Zinc","dose":"50 mg QD"},{"agent":"Folic acid and cod liver oil","why":"Mucosal membrane and immune restoration."},{"agent":"Multimineral compound","why":"High in chromium, manganese, potassium, zinc and selenium."},{"agent":"Centella asiatica (gotu kola) tincture","dose":"15 drops QD","why":"Promotes cognitive focus and repairs mucosal barriers."},{"agent":"Physical medicine","why":"Lumbar spinal manipulation; a 3 mm shoe lift on the right shoe for an anatomical discrepancy."}]}],"patient":"30-year-old female"},{"id":"case59","n":59,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Pre-Diabetic Dysglycemia","condition":"Prediabetes","presentation":"Right upper quadrant discomfort, brittle nails, alopecia, and postprandial glucose dipping to 58 mg/dL on a glucose tolerance test.","sections":[{"name":"Trace mineral protocol","items":[{"agent":"Chromium, manganese and potassium aspartate","dose":"Daily"},{"agent":"High-potency vitamin B-complex"},{"agent":"Gymnema sylvestre tincture","dose":"30 drops QD"},{"agent":"Dietary shift","why":"Discontinuation of continuous snacking; three structured meals rich in lean poultry and lamb, with snacking exclusively on nut butters — almond, cashew."}]}],"patient":"43-year-old female"},{"id":"case60","n":60,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Reactive Postprandial Hypoglycemia","condition":"Hypoglycemia","presentation":"Severe hypoglycemic crashes following simple sugar consumption; onychoschizia (splitting nails), tinea unguium, and an elevated MCV at 98 fL.","sections":[{"name":"Prescription","items":[{"agent":"Total elimination of simple sucrose and glucose"},{"agent":"Meal structure","why":"Three balanced meals daily plus a mandatory 3:00 PM protein snack."},{"agent":"Super EPA and flaxseed oil","dose":"1 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Vitamin K1","why":"Fortification for dry cracked feet."},{"agent":"Multimineral with chromium","dose":"200 mcg daily"},{"agent":"Corynanthe yohimbe tincture","dose":"7 drops BID","why":"Alpha-2 adrenergic antagonist for metabolic thermogenesis and weight reduction."},{"agent":"Hydroxy-folate drops","why":"Sublingual vitamin B12 and folinic acid for the elevated MCV."},{"agent":"Tea tree oil ointment","why":"Applied topically to the fungal nails."}]}],"patient":"56-year-old female","caution":"Yohimbe raises blood pressure and heart rate, provokes anxiety and panic, and interacts with MAO inhibitors, SSRIs and stimulants; it is contraindicated in hypertension, anxiety disorder and renal disease."},{"id":"case61","n":61,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Primary Hypothyroidism with Cold Intolerance","condition":"Hypothyroidism","presentation":"Severe cold intolerance, memory fog, arthralgias, asthma, and serum T4 depressed at 4.8 mcg/dL.","sections":[{"name":"Integrative protocol","items":[{"agent":"Levothyroxine (Synthroid)","dose":"75 mcg QD","why":"Swiftly restored temperature tolerance and cognitive clarity."},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID","why":"Allowed complete discontinuation of asthma inhalers and weaning of NSAIDs."},{"agent":"Complete dairy exclusion","why":"Removal of all bovine milk products to arrest the underlying allergic asthma."},{"agent":"Silybum marianum","dose":"500 mg BID"},{"agent":"Shark cartilage","dose":"2 capsules BID","why":"For articular inflammation."},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Long-term tapering plan","why":"Introduce kelp (iodine) and thyroid protomorphogens while slowly tapering synthetic T4."}]}],"patient":"35-year-old male","also":["Asthma"],"caution":"Tapering levothyroxine in primary hypothyroidism is done on serial TSH and free T4, not on symptoms; kelp adds an uncontrolled iodine dose on top of a replacement thyroid hormone."},{"id":"case62","n":62,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Subclinical Hypothyroidism","condition":"Hypothyroidism","presentation":"Generalised burning pruritus after hot baths, left lower back paresthesia, constipation, fatigue, and a low-normal T4 at 5.6 mcg/dL.","sections":[{"name":"Glandular protomorphogen protocol","items":[{"agent":"Thyroid protomorphogen extract","dose":"3 capsules at lunch"},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid","dose":"250 mg QD"},{"agent":"Selenium","dose":"200 mcg QD","why":"Essential for peripheral iodothyronine 5'-deiodinase conversion of T4 to active T3."},{"agent":"Cod liver oil and carotenes","why":"Mucosal and dermal barrier repair."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg QD"}]}],"patient":"35-year-old female","caution":"Desiccated thyroid and “protomorphogen” glandulars vary in hormone content between batches and can suppress TSH; they are not an inert nutritional support."},{"id":"case63","n":63,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"“Sluggish Pancreas Syndrome” (Dyssynergic Insulin / Glucagon Secretion)","condition":"Hypoglycemia","presentation":"Dysglycemia with slow glucagon release and delayed glucose clearance, systemic candidiasis, high-volume athletic exhaustion, and severe premenstrual depression.","sections":[{"name":"Endocrine & bitter botanical protocol","items":[{"agent":"Chromium","dose":"200–400 mcg QD"},{"agent":"Syzygium jambolana (jambul)","dose":"20 drops BID","why":"Blunts acute postprandial glucose surges."},{"agent":"Camellia sinensis (green tea) infusions","why":"Pancreatic antioxidant defence."},{"agent":"Cola nitida (kola nut) powder","dose":"¼ tsp in water, maximum 3 cups daily","why":"Replacing coffee."},{"agent":"Pancreatic secretory tonics","dose":"Before meals","why":"Equal parts Achillea millefolium (yarrow) and Chionanthus virginicus (fringe tree)."}]},{"name":"Premenstrual regimen","items":[{"agent":"Vitamin B6","dose":"50 mg QD"},{"agent":"Vitamin B12"},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra root tea","why":"Inhibits beta-reductase activity."}]}],"patient":"39-year-old female","also":["Candidiasis","Premenstrual syndrome"]},{"id":"case64","n":64,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Hyperparathyroidism & Recurrent Nephrolithiasis","condition":"Hyperparathyroidism","presentation":"Recurrent calcium oxalate nephrolithiasis, secondary transitional cell bladder carcinoma, hypercalcemia at 11.4 mg/dL, depressed vitamin D, and a parathyroid adenoma.","sections":[{"name":"Acute nephrolithiasis & calcium protocol","items":[{"agent":"Dietary calcium restriction","why":"Immediate cessation of calcium-dense foods and supplements."},{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"200 mg TID"},{"agent":"Litholytic botanical formula","dose":"120 drops TID","why":"1 part Hydrangea arborescens (hydrangea root) and 1 part Ammi visnaga (khella) — spasmolytic to ureteral smooth muscle."},{"agent":"D-mannose","why":"Bladder epithelial protection."},{"agent":"Definitive treatment","why":"Surgical parathyroidectomy, indicated for functional parathyroid neoplasia."}]}],"patient":"62-year-old male","also":["Kidney stones"],"caution":"Ammi visnaga is a low-dose botanical and is phototoxic. Restricting dietary calcium in calcium oxalate stone disease increases oxalate absorption and is now generally advised against."},{"id":"case65","n":65,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Pituitary Prolactinoma","condition":"Prolactinoma","presentation":"A suprasellar microadenoma with secondary amenorrhea, persistent galactorrhea, severe bitemporal visual field loss, and serum prolactin spiking from 300 to over 600 ng/mL.","sections":[{"name":"Dopaminergic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Bromocriptine mesylate","dose":"1.25 mg with a snack at bedtime, titrated up to 2.5 mg TID","why":"Or a modern dopamine agonist such as cabergoline (Dostinex), to shrink the prolactin-secreting tumour mass."},{"agent":"Hydrocortisone","dose":"20–30 mg daily","why":"Supportive medical coverage."}]}],"patient":"27-year-old female","also":["Amenorrhea"],"caution":"Bitemporal field loss means the adenoma is compressing the optic chiasm — this is a neurosurgical and endocrinological referral, and the medication is prescribed and monitored, not self-managed."},{"id":"case66","n":66,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Benign Thyroid Cysts","condition":"Thyroid nodules and cysts","presentation":"Palpable right lobar thyroid enlargement, paraspinal burning sensations, alternating bowel habits, pan-mineral depletion on hair analysis, and a normal serum T4.","sections":[{"name":"Thyroid glandular regimen","items":[{"agent":"Thyro Forte (thyroid protomorphogen)","dose":"2 capsules QAM"},{"agent":"High-potency multivitamin and multimineral","dose":"1 daily of each"},{"agent":"Silybum marianum","dose":"2 capsules BID"}]}],"patient":"39-year-old female","caution":"A palpable thyroid nodule is worked up with ultrasound and, where indicated, fine-needle aspiration before it is treated as benign."},{"id":"case67","n":67,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Benign Thyroid Colloid Nodule","condition":"Thyroid nodules and cysts","presentation":"Palpable anterior cervical enlargement with a neck circumference of 37.5 cm causing tracheal compression, severe anxiety, and vasomotor hot flashes.","sections":[{"name":"Nodule protocol","items":[{"agent":"Potassium iodide (Tri-Quench)","dose":"4 drops QD"},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"¼ tsp QID"},{"agent":"Boron","dose":"1 mg TID","why":"Suppresses vasomotor hot flashes."},{"agent":"Botanical tincture","dose":"15 drops BID","why":"Equal parts Mitchella repens and Angelica sinensis (1:5 extracts)."},{"agent":"Levothyroxine","dose":"25 mcg QD","why":"Low dose, to suppress endogenous TSH drive."},{"agent":"Surgical resection","why":"Indicated if tracheal compression persists."}]}],"patient":"46-year-old female","also":["Menopause"]},{"id":"case68","n":68,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"TSH-Refractory Thyroidopathy","condition":"Hypothyroidism","presentation":"Paradoxically elevated T4 with a high-normal TSH, dry skin, memory loss, fatigue, and a history of childhood rheumatic carditis and severe streptococcal sepsis.","sections":[{"name":"Receptor sensitising regimen","items":[{"agent":"Desiccated thyroid extract","dose":"Continue 3 grains QAM"},{"agent":"Adrenal protomorphogen","dose":"2 capsules QAM"},{"agent":"Ovary glandular protomorphogen","why":"Cycle-specific dosing for PMS."},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid and vitamin C","dose":"Vitamin C 1000 mg QD"},{"agent":"Quercetin and DGL","why":"Autoimmune allergy suppression."},{"agent":"Streptococcinum 200X homeopathic","why":"Intermittent constitutional nosode addressing early childhood post-streptococcal priming."}]}],"patient":"Adult female","also":["Rheumatic fever"],"caution":"An elevated T4 with a non-suppressed TSH is the pattern of a TSH-secreting adenoma or thyroid hormone resistance; it warrants pituitary imaging rather than more thyroid hormone."},{"id":"case69","n":69,"chapter":"Endocrinology","title":"Thyrotoxicosis & Graves' Disease","condition":"Hyperthyroidism","presentation":"Marked exophthalmos, upper lid lag, a hyperdynamic precordium with a high-pitched systolic apex squeak, a systolic bruit and thrill over a diffuse thyroid goiter, resting heart rate 136 bpm, T4 21.4 mcg/dL, fine digital tremor, and pretibial myxedema.","sections":[{"name":"Allopathic stabilisation (pre-surgical)","text":"Tapazole (methimazole) titrated to 20 mg QID; converted in hospital to propylthiouracil paired with Inderal (propranolol 20 mg QID) to blunt the adrenergic storm prior to total thyroidectomy."},{"name":"Post-thyroidectomy hormone replacement","items":[{"agent":"Levothyroxine (Synthroid)","dose":"0.1 mg QD titrated rapidly to 0.2 mg QD","why":"To resolve profound post-surgical hypothyroidism — T4 had collapsed to 1.2 mcg/dL and T7 to 0.23."}]}],"patient":"17-year-old female","caution":"Untreated thyrotoxicosis at this severity can tip into thyroid storm, which is fatal without urgent care. This case is recorded as conventional management for exactly that reason."},{"id":"case70","n":70,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Acute Amebiasis (Entamoeba histolytica)","condition":"Parasites, intestinal","presentation":"Watery diarrhea persisting for a month, right lower quadrant aching, McBurney's point tenderness, and an elevated MCV at 100 fL.","sections":[{"name":"Amoebicidal protocol","items":[{"agent":"Antiparasitic botanical extract","dose":"60 drops TID for 5 consecutive days","why":"1 part Spigelia anthelmia and 1 part Berberis aquifolium."},{"agent":"Artemisia annua (sweet Annie) capsules","dose":"1000 mg BID–TID for 7 days"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Probiotics","dose":"2 capsules at bedtime"},{"agent":"Dietary protocol","why":"Strict elimination of simple sugars and dairy for 30 days."}]},{"name":"Epithelial mucilages","items":[{"agent":"Cabbage juice","dose":"½ cup BID"},{"agent":"Ulmus fulva (slippery elm)","dose":"1 tsp TID"},{"agent":"Althaea officinalis","dose":"2 capsules TID"}]}],"patient":"32-year-old female","caution":"Invasive amebiasis can seed a liver abscess and needs confirmed eradication; right lower quadrant pain with McBurney's tenderness also has to exclude appendicitis before it is treated as a parasite."},{"id":"case71","n":71,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Ascariasis (Ascaris lumbricoides)","condition":"Parasites, intestinal","presentation":"Visible passage of roundworms, chronic abdominal bloat, alternating diarrhea, left hypochondriac tension, and an elevated SGPT at 64 U/L.","sections":[{"name":"Vermifugal protocol","items":[{"agent":"Botanical anthelmintic","dose":"90 drops TID for 3 consecutive days","why":"Equal parts Spigelia anthelmintica and Artemisia annua."},{"agent":"Bromelain","dose":"1500 mg TID between meals","why":"Proteolytic destruction of helminth cuticles."},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp TID"},{"agent":"Probiotics","dose":"2 capsules at bedtime"}]},{"name":"Pharmacological alternative","text":"Mebendazole 100 mg orally BID for 3 days, or piperazine citrate 75 mg/kg orally QD for 2 days to a maximum of 3.5 g/day."}],"patient":"33-year-old male","caution":"Spigelia is a low-dose botanical with cardiac and neurological toxicity in overdose. A heavy Ascaris burden can obstruct the bowel or migrate into the biliary tree when the worms are irritated rather than killed outright."},{"id":"case72","n":72,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Barrett's Esophagus","condition":"Barrett's esophagus","presentation":"Longstanding erosive gastroesophageal reflux causing columnar metaplasia of the distal esophageal squamous mucosa; status post cholecystectomy with postoperative abdominal wall wound complications.","sections":[{"name":"Mucosal repair & anti-metaplastic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"2 capsules BID","why":"Essential for lowering local tissue inflammation."},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tsp BID","why":"Promotes microvascular capillary restoration."},{"agent":"Acidophilus","dose":"2 capsules at bedtime"},{"agent":"Glucosamine sulfate","dose":"1000 mg BID","why":"Glycosaminoglycan synthesis for the mucosal basement lining."},{"agent":"Kelp","dose":"2 capsules at breakfast and 2 at dinner"},{"agent":"CoQ10","dose":"100 mg QD"},{"agent":"Thorne Basic Nutrients V","why":"Comprehensive micronutrient base."},{"agent":"Dietary exclusions","why":"Total elimination of wheat, gluten and cheeses; small meal volumes to prevent intra-gastric pressure spikes."}]}],"patient":"67-year-old female","also":["GERD"],"caution":"Barrett's is a premalignant lesion and stays under endoscopic surveillance on an interval set by the degree of dysplasia, whatever else is added."},{"id":"case73","n":73,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Blastocystis hominis Colitis","condition":"Parasites, intestinal","presentation":"Severe protozoal enteritis, nausea, a 15 lb weight loss, severe dehydration requiring intravenous saline infusions, and intolerance to metronidazole (Flagyl).","sections":[{"name":"Enteric eradication protocol","items":[{"agent":"Antimicrobial botanical tincture","dose":"60 drops TID","why":"Equal parts Berberis aquifolium, Hydrastis canadensis, Achillea millefolium, Spigelia marilandica and Gentiana lutea."},{"agent":"Robert's Formula Plus","dose":"2 capsules TID"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg TID","why":"Calms severe enteric mucosal inflammation."},{"agent":"DGL powder","why":"Soothing demulcent."}]}],"patient":"26-year-old female"},{"id":"case74","n":74,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Gastrointestinal Candidiasis","condition":"Candidiasis","presentation":"Chronic abdominal distention, gas, raw stomach irritation, and a stool culture demonstrating 2+ Candida, 4+ E. coli, and an absence of fecal bile.","sections":[{"name":"Antifungal & mucosal healing protocol","items":[{"agent":"Caprylic acid","dose":"Oral"},{"agent":"Lomatium dissectum tincture","dose":"8 drops TID for 14 days"},{"agent":"Stellaria media (chickweed) capsules","why":"Emollient to soothe ulcerated and raw gut surfaces."},{"agent":"Quercetin and magnesium","dose":"Magnesium 200 mg QD","why":"Enteric smooth muscle antispasmodic."},{"agent":"Lactobacillus acidophilus","dose":"High potency","why":"Repopulation."},{"agent":"Dietary protocol","why":"No simple sugars; a macronutrient split of 20% fat, 40% clean protein and 40% complex fibre and carbohydrate."},{"agent":"GABA and glycine powder","dose":"At night","why":"To quiet nocturnal brain arousal."}]}],"patient":"37-year-old male","caution":"Lomatium is the botanical whose whole-body rash is documented elsewhere in this casebook; start low and stop at the first sign of an exanthem."},{"id":"case75","n":75,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Celiac Sprue","condition":"Celiac disease","presentation":"Intractable chronic diarrhea with 10–12 watery evacuations daily, severe peripheral pitting edema, refractory hypochromic anemia despite oral iron, hypotension at 90/50 mmHg, and severe villous blunting.","sections":[{"name":"Mucosal restoration & barrier repair","items":[{"agent":"Strict gluten elimination","why":"Absolute removal of wheat, rye, barley, spelt and kamut."},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg TID","why":"Stabilises hyper-permeable mucosal gut-associated lymphoid tissue."},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp TID"},{"agent":"Aloe vera pure inner leaf juice","dose":"½ oz BID"},{"agent":"Matricaria recutita (chamomile) tea or tincture","why":"Intestinal antispasmodic and antibacterial."},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp QD","why":"Repairs damaged villous capillary architecture."},{"agent":"Lactobacillus acidophilus / Bifidobacterium","dose":"Nightly at bedtime"},{"agent":"Secondary exclusions","why":"Complete elimination of dairy, margarine and commercial greasy foods."}]},{"name":"Enteric melatonin considerations","items":[{"agent":"Melatonin","dose":"Up to 3 mg QHS","why":"Acts as an enterochromaffin-derived paracrine hormone that scavenges reactive oxygen species, regulates gastric motility and blunts intestinal hyperalgesia."}]}],"patient":"33-year-old female"},{"id":"case76","n":76,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Early-Stage Hepatic Cirrhosis","condition":"Hepatic cirrhosis","presentation":"Alcohol-induced early cirrhosis; hepatomegaly 20% enlarged and tender; AST 74 U/L, ALT 146 U/L, GGT 146 U/L, thrombocytopenia with platelets at 104,000/µL, and a dry, cracked tongue showing yin deficiency.","sections":[{"name":"Anti-fibrotic & hepatoprotective protocol","items":[{"agent":"Bromelain and curcumin 50/50 compound","dose":"2 capsules TID","why":"Bromelain provides systemic fibrinolytic activity against developing hepatic collagenous scars; curcumin arrests parenchymal lipid peroxidation."},{"agent":"Silybum marianum (milk thistle)","dose":"2 capsules BID"},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp before meals","why":"Gastric acid protection."},{"agent":"Vitamin A","dose":"10,000 IU QD","why":"Re-supplies depleted hepatic stellate (Ito) cells to halt myofibroblastic transformation."},{"agent":"Vitamin C and vitamin E","dose":"Vitamin C 1000 mg BID, vitamin E 800 IU QD"},{"agent":"Digestive enzyme tablets","dose":"2 per meal","why":"To compensate for depressed digestive output."},{"agent":"Dietary protocol","why":"A complete ban on alcohol, NSAIDs and fried fats; frequent small meals to reduce portal hepatic workload."},{"agent":"Relaxation","dose":"2 minutes daily","why":"Controlled parasympathetic diaphragmatic breathing — nasal inhale, oral exhale, shoulders dropping."}]}],"patient":"40-year-old female","caution":"Vitamin A is cleared by the liver and is itself hepatotoxic in cirrhosis; thrombocytopenia here signals portal hypertension, and bromelain and vitamin E add antiplatelet effect on top of it."},{"id":"case77","n":77,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Profound Episodic Spastic Colitis & Crohn's Disease","condition":"Inflammatory bowel disease","presentation":"Severe periodic semi-annual colonic spasm causing acute functional pseudo-obstruction, intractable vomiting every 15 minutes for 16 continuous hours, and adrenal burnout.","sections":[{"name":"Colonic spasmolytic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"200 mg BID, titrated up to bowel tolerance","why":"To halt smooth-muscle hyper-contraction."},{"agent":"N-acetyl-glucosamine (NAG)","why":"Inhibits lectin binding and rebuilds the intestinal glycosaminoglycan layer."},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp TID"},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Vitamin B12","dose":"Monthly parenteral injection"},{"agent":"Dietary strategy","why":"Low-residue cooked foods — yams, squash, pureed split-pea soup, well-steamed greens, fish, poultry; absolute avoidance of all whole nuts, seeds, coarse whole grains, cow's milk dairy and wheat."}]}],"patient":"41-year-old female"},{"id":"case78","n":78,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Regional Colitis of the Ascending Colon","condition":"Inflammatory bowel disease","presentation":"Recurrent right-sided pulsating abdominal pain localised over the ascending colon, with an elevated white cell count at 12,100/µL and ESR at 16 mm/hr.","sections":[{"name":"Prescription","items":[{"agent":"Stellaria media (chickweed) capsules","dose":"1 capsule TID"},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp TID"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1 capsule TID"},{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"2 capsules QPM","why":"Relaxes colonic circular smooth muscle."},{"agent":"Musculoskeletal adjuncts","why":"Thoracolumbar spinal manipulation; Rhus toxicodendron 12X; Ligaplex."}]}],"patient":"Adult male"},{"id":"case79","n":79,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Long-Term Colonic Irrigation Support","condition":"Constipation","presentation":"Chronically altered colonic transit with mucosal hyperemia above 10 cm on sigmoidoscopy, managed with bi-weekly colonic hydrotherapy for over 25 years.","sections":[{"name":"Maintenance protocol","items":[{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"Daily each morning","why":"To suppress mucosal inflammation."},{"agent":"Lactobacillus acidophilus","dose":"2 capsules QHS following irrigations"},{"agent":"Crataegus spp. berry solid extract","dose":"½ tsp QD","why":"Preserves colonic mucosal capillary integrity."},{"agent":"Ruscus aculeatus","dose":"60 drops BID","why":"Venous and mesenteric circulation."},{"agent":"Pancreatin glandular protomorphogen","dose":"3 tablets with meals"},{"agent":"Barley green juice","dose":"Daily","why":"Alkaline mineral drink."}]}],"patient":"Elderly female","caution":"Decades of twice-weekly colonic irrigation carries its own risks — electrolyte disturbance, perforation, and dependence; this case records maintenance of an existing practice, not a recommendation to begin one."},{"id":"case80","n":80,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Ulcerative Colitis Co-Managed with Prednisone","condition":"Inflammatory bowel disease","presentation":"Severe pancolitis flare, hematochezia, severe microcytic anemia with haematocrit plunging to 21–27% and requiring transfusion, high-dose prednisone dependency, and confirmed severe IgG dairy and wheat allergy.","sections":[{"name":"Anti-inflammatory & hematinic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"Titrated from ½ tsp BID to ½ tsp TID"},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"Titrated from ½ tsp TID to ½ tsp QID"},{"agent":"Robert's Formula","dose":"2 capsules TID"},{"agent":"Musa paradisiaca (plantain banana) fruit powder","dose":"2 capsules BID","why":"An active mucosal barrier emollient."},{"agent":"Fresh raw cabbage juice","dose":"1 full cup daily","why":"Supplies S-methylmethionine (vitamin U)."},{"agent":"N-acetyl-cysteine (NAC)","dose":"⅛ tsp QD","why":"Strips inflammatory dietary wheat agglutinins from the mucosal surface."},{"agent":"Rumex crispus (yellow dock)","dose":"2 capsules daily","why":"Gentle organic iron accretion."},{"agent":"Supplemental liquid iron drops","dose":"½ tsp BID","why":"Supplying 50 mg elemental iron."},{"agent":"Arsenicum album 12X homeopathic","dose":"2 pellets QPM"},{"agent":"Croton tiglium 6X homeopathic","why":"Used post-surgically to reduce frequent loose evacuations following ileoanal pull-through anastomosis."}]}],"patient":"Adult male","caution":"Prednisone is never stopped abruptly after long-term use — adrenal suppression makes the taper a medical one. A haematocrit in the low 20s with ongoing bleeding is a transfusion decision, not a supplement one."},{"id":"case81","n":81,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Chronic Hypotonic Constipation","condition":"Constipation","presentation":"Bowel movements occurring only with heavy caffeine stimulation, an elevated haematocrit at 44.4% from chronic dehydration, and premenstrual dysphoria.","sections":[{"name":"Bowel retraining regimen","items":[{"agent":"Potassium and magnesium aspartate","dose":"1 capsule AM and 1 PM, titrated to 2 capsules BID","why":"80 mg potassium and 80 mg magnesium per capsule."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg TID, taken to bowel tolerance"},{"agent":"Dioctyl sodium sulfosuccinate (DSS)","dose":"100 mg QD","why":"Temporary stool surfactant."},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra solid extract and pantothenic acid","dose":"Licorice ¼ tsp QD, pantothenic acid 500 mg QD"},{"agent":"Silybum marianum tincture","dose":"60 drops BID"},{"agent":"Dietary rehydration","why":"Mandatory marked elevation of pure fluid intake plus whole oat bran cereal daily."}]}],"patient":"30-year-old female"},{"id":"case82","n":82,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Pediatric Constipation with Magnesium Deficiency","condition":"Constipation","presentation":"Lifelong constipation dating to infancy — evacuations once every 10 days as a neonate — with hard, dry scybala, Dennie-Morgan infraorbital lines, and profound hair magnesium depletion at 11.8 ppm against a normal 39–148 ppm.","sections":[{"name":"Trace mineral protocol","items":[{"agent":"Hypoallergenic pediatric multimineral","dose":"3 capsules daily for 14 days, then 3 capsules every other day","why":"Delivering about 300 mg elemental magnesium, 300 mg calcium, 20 mg zinc, 150 mcg selenium, 6 mg manganese, 200 mcg chromium, 90 mg potassium and 100 mcg iodine."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"500 mg BID"},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"1 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Human microflora probiotics","dose":"1 capsule nightly"},{"agent":"Dietary exclusion","why":"Complete exclusion of cow's milk dairy and commercial hot dogs."}]}],"patient":"7-year-old male","caution":"Constipation from birth with delayed passage of meconium is Hirschsprung disease until excluded — the rectal suction biopsy comes before a mineral protocol."},{"id":"case83","n":83,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Post-Surgical Constipation","condition":"Constipation","presentation":"Complete cessation of normal peristalsis following emergent laparotomy for a ruptured ovarian cyst and appendectomy.","sections":[{"name":"Cathartic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Plantago ovata (blond psyllium seed husks)","dose":"1 rounded tsp TID (5.4 g TID), tapered over two weeks to 2 tsp QD, then 1 tsp QD","why":"Mixed vigorously into a large glass of pure water."},{"agent":"Magnesium","dose":"200 mg BID"},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg BID"}]},{"name":"Alternative European botanical laxative compound (Aboca formula)","items":[{"agent":"Compound","dose":"60 drops, or 2 capsules, at bedtime","why":"4 parts Cassia angustifolia (senna), 2 parts Aloe vera, 2 parts Taraxacum officinale (dandelion root), 1 part Cichorium intybus (chicory), 1 part Foeniculum vulgare (fennel), 1 part Carum carvi (caraway), 0.5 part Peumus boldus (boldo), 0.5 part Cuminum cyminum (cumin)."}]}],"patient":"Adult female","caution":"Bulk-forming psyllium is contraindicated while a post-operative ileus or obstruction is still possible — peristalsis has to be confirmed present first. Stimulant anthraquinone laxatives are for short-term use only."},{"id":"case84","n":84,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Crohn's Disease with Transmural Colonic Involvement","condition":"Inflammatory bowel disease","presentation":"A 12-year history of transmural colitis, ulceration, cramping, hematochezia and past nephrolithiasis, while taking azathioprine (Imuran), prednisone and mesalamine (Pentasa).","sections":[{"name":"Anti-cytokine botanical & mucosal protocol","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1500 mg BID","why":"Blocks mucosal NF-kB and lipoxygenase pathways."},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"1 full tsp powder each morning"},{"agent":"Fruit anthocyanins concentrate","dose":"1 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Robert's Formula","dose":"2 capsules AM and 2 capsules PM","why":"Geranium maculatum (astringent and hemostatic), Althaea officinalis root (mucilage), Hydrastis canadensis root (berberine suppresses IL-8 secretion and repairs mucosal architecture), Brassica oleracea (cabbage) and Echinacea angustifolia."}]}],"patient":"39-year-old male","outcome":"Completely weaned off all pharmaceutical agents within 60 days under medical supervision, remaining symptom-free for over 3 years.","caution":"The weaning described was physician-supervised. Stopping azathioprine or prednisone independently risks a severe flare and, with steroids, adrenal crisis."},{"id":"case85","n":85,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Acute Infectious Diarrhea with Upper Respiratory Catarrh","condition":"Diarrhea","presentation":"Acute profuse watery diarrhea for 7 days with low fever, an allergic contact armpit rash, and copious rhinorrhea.","sections":[{"name":"Prescription","items":[{"agent":"Croton tiglium 6X homeopathic","dose":"3 pellets TID","why":"Rapidly arrests choleraic watery diarrhea."},{"agent":"Glycyrrhiza glabra tincture","dose":"60 drops BID for 7 days, dropping to 30 drops QD for 3 weeks"},{"agent":"L-lysine","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Euphrasia officinalis (eyebright) 1:1 fluid extract","dose":"3 mL (90 drops) TID","why":"Astringent to the mucous membranes."}]}],"patient":"26-year-old male"},{"id":"case86","n":86,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Chronic Diarrhea with Corn Hypersensitivity","condition":"Diarrhea","presentation":"Intractable chronic loose stools, severe abdominal bloat, hypertension at 170/100 mmHg, and cytotoxic allergy confirmation to corn and cornstarch additives.","sections":[{"name":"Prescription","items":[{"agent":"Dietary elimination","why":"Total elimination of corn syrup, corn derivatives, dairy, eggs and coffee."},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"¼ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Corynanthe yohimbe tincture","dose":"6 drops BID","why":"For metabolic weight loss."},{"agent":"Natrum sulphuricum 6X homeopathic","why":"Specifically indicated for morning-aggravated loose stools with hepatobiliary congestion."},{"agent":"Glycine powder","dose":"1 level tsp PRN","why":"For nervous intestinal cramping."},{"agent":"Magnesium trisilicate","dose":"PRN","why":"For gastric pyrosis."}]}],"patient":"70-year-old female","also":["Food intolerance"],"caution":"Yohimbe raises blood pressure — giving it to a patient sitting at 170/100 mmHg is the one element of this case that should not be reproduced."},{"id":"case87","n":87,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Dientamoeba fragilis & Pinworm Enteric Infection","condition":"Parasites, intestinal","presentation":"Pruritus ani and lower abdominal cramping after failure of iodoquinol (Yodoxin); stool positive for Dientamoeba fragilis, Entamoeba coli and Enterobius vermicularis.","sections":[{"name":"Antiparasitic protocol","items":[{"agent":"Artemisia annua (sweet Annie)","dose":"500 mg TID for 5 consecutive days"},{"agent":"Althaea officinalis (marshmallow)","dose":"1 capsule BID"},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Quercetin","why":"Mucosal anti-inflammatory support."},{"agent":"Silybum marianum","why":"Liver protection during protozoal die-off."}]},{"name":"Alternative pinworm & protozoal therapies","items":[{"agent":"Cina 3X homeopathic","dose":"3 pellets TID"},{"agent":"Spigelia, Quassia amara, or Robert's Formula","dose":"Robert's Formula dosed aggressively at 3 capsules QID for 5 days"}]}],"patient":"27-year-old female","caution":"Pinworm reinfects through the household; treating the index patient without treating contacts and laundering bedding is what makes it recur."},{"id":"case88","n":88,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Postprandial Fatigue & Food Intolerance","condition":"Food intolerance","presentation":"Severe somnolence after lunch, low-normal blood pressure at 100/52 mmHg, and a borderline T4 at 6.6 mcg/dL.","sections":[{"name":"Protocol","items":[{"agent":"Sublingual hydroxy-folate drops","dose":"6 drops QD","why":"Vitamin B12 with folinic acid."},{"agent":"Lactobacillus acidophilus","dose":"2 capsules QHS"},{"agent":"DGL powder and licorice root tea","dose":"DGL ½ tsp TID"},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"¼ tsp TID"},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg at breakfast"},{"agent":"Dietary balancing","why":"Elimination of peanuts, wheat and pizza; reallocation of calories from heavy lunches to balanced breakfasts; extra salt added to meals to raise blood pressure."}]}],"patient":"55-year-old male"},{"id":"case89","n":89,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Duodenal Peptic Ulcer","condition":"Peptic ulcer disease","presentation":"A radiographically confirmed ulcer crater in the duodenal bulb near the pyloric sphincter, severe hunger pains, hyperchlorhydria, and Maalox abuse.","sections":[{"name":"Duodenal mucosal protective protocol","items":[{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"2 capsules TID strictly on an empty stomach before meals"},{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Trigelco","dose":"PRN for burning pain","why":"Magnesium trisilicate and natural gastric mucin tablets."},{"agent":"N-acetyl-cysteine (NAC)","dose":"Low dose","why":"Reduces dietary wheat mucosal antigenicity."},{"agent":"Dietary carotenes","why":"High intake of yellow and orange squashes, yams and carrots."},{"agent":"Cessation","why":"Complete cessation of coffee, alcohol and chocolate."}]}],"patient":"30-year-old male","caution":"Duodenal ulcer is tested for H. pylori and eradicated where positive; melena or haematemesis is an emergency."},{"id":"case90","n":90,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Non-Ulcer Dyspepsia","condition":"Dyspepsia","presentation":"Chronic epigastric burning, nocturnal churning and early satiety, with normal upper and lower GI endoscopies.","sections":[{"name":"Prescription","items":[{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp AM and PM"},{"agent":"Quercetin powder","dose":"½ tsp QD"},{"agent":"Magnesium and potassium aspartate","why":"Visceral antispasmodic support."},{"agent":"Digestive enzymes","dose":"1 capsule with each meal"},{"agent":"Glycine powder","dose":"At bedtime","why":"Relaxes gastrointestinal neuromuscular tone."},{"agent":"Dietary exclusion","why":"Complete exclusion of fried fats, dark poultry meat, eggs and peanut butter."}]}],"patient":"30-year-old male"},{"id":"case91","n":91,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Pediatric Eosinophilic Enteropathy","condition":"Eosinophilic enteropathy","presentation":"Chronic diffuse postprandial abdominal cramping, submandibular lymphadenopathy, and peripheral eosinophilia elevated to 7%.","sections":[{"name":"Alterative & digestive protocol","items":[{"agent":"Alterative lymph compound","dose":"30 drops per meal","why":"Equal parts Arctium lappa root and Berberis aquifolium (1:5 extracts)."},{"agent":"Endogenous acid stimulation","dose":"3 minutes before meals","why":"1 tsp apple cider vinegar in ½ oz water with 7 drops Gentiana lutea tincture."},{"agent":"Adrenal glandular protomorphogen","dose":"Daily"},{"agent":"Dietary elimination","why":"Removal of commercial sodas, burgers, processed cheeses and wheat-heavy bakery goods."}]}],"patient":"17-year-old male"},{"id":"case92","n":92,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Adolescent Food Hypersensitivity Enteropathy","condition":"Food intolerance","presentation":"Immediate postprandial exhaustion, chronic periumbilical ache, recurrent cephalalgia, and Dennie-Morgan allergic shiners.","sections":[{"name":"Prescription","items":[{"agent":"Dietary overhaul","why":"Total removal of wheat and dairy; replacement with steel-cut oats, organic soups, and corn-tortilla chicken and bean burritos."},{"agent":"Vitamin C","dose":"1000 mg BID"},{"agent":"Vitamin E","dose":"400 IU QD"},{"agent":"Balanced multimineral and hypoallergenic multivitamin"},{"agent":"Quercetin","dose":"1000 mg BID"}]}],"patient":"15-year-old female"},{"id":"case93","n":93,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Upper / Lower Intestinal Maldigestion & Meteorism","condition":"Bloating and gas","presentation":"Severe flatulence and bloating, hypochlorhydria, multiple IgG food allergies, and a history of duodenitis.","sections":[{"name":"Protocol","items":[{"agent":"Betaine HCl with pancreatic enzymes","dose":"1 capsule per meal"},{"agent":"Pancreatic protomorphogen","dose":"3 capsules QD"},{"agent":"Homeopathic allergen compound","dose":"5 drops sublingually QD","why":"The offending foods prepared in a 6X potency."},{"agent":"Pantothenic acid","dose":"250 mg QD"},{"agent":"Selenium and vitamin C","dose":"Selenium 200 mcg QD, vitamin C 1000 mg QD"},{"agent":"Clinical escalation","why":"Oregano oil for secondary fungal blooms if the meteorism resists enzyme therapy."}]}],"patient":"32-year-old female","caution":"Betaine HCl on a background of duodenitis can reproduce the ulcer pain it is meant to relieve; it is stopped, not pushed through, if burning appears."},{"id":"case94","n":94,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Stress-Induced Pediatric Gastralgia","condition":"Dyspepsia","presentation":"Periumbilical and epigastric cramping corresponding to a school transition and a dietary reliance on dairy and wheat.","sections":[{"name":"Pediatric demulcent & antispasmodic protocol","items":[{"agent":"DGL powder","dose":"½ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Foeniculum vulgare (fennel)","why":"Warm seed tea."},{"agent":"Flaxseed oil","dose":"1 tbsp QD"},{"agent":"Cod liver oil","dose":"2 pearls QD"},{"agent":"Dietary shift","why":"Transition from refined wheat cereals to oatmeal, rice cakes, and diversified grains — millet, quinoa, wild rice."}]}],"patient":"9-year-old male"},{"id":"case95","n":95,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Antenatal & Postnatal Gastroschisis Support","condition":"Gastroschisis","presentation":"Antenatal ultrasound diagnosis at 8 months gestation showing a complete abdominal wall fissure with intestinal herniation.","sections":[{"name":"Integrative surgical support protocol","items":[{"agent":"Maternal prenatal optimisation","why":"Whole-food organic nutrition rich in complex minerals and unrefined sea salt."},{"agent":"Symphytum officinale (comfrey) extract","dose":"A few drops daily in water orally","why":"Immediate post-surgical neonatal."},{"agent":"Stellaria media (chickweed) extract","dose":"A few drops daily in water orally"},{"agent":"Arnica montana 12X homeopathic","dose":"Sublingually","why":"To accelerate surgical tissue repair."}]}],"patient":"Neonate","caution":"Comfrey contains hepatotoxic pyrrolizidine alkaloids and is not given internally, least of all to a neonate. Gastroschisis is a surgical emergency at birth and this is adjunctive support only."},{"id":"case96","n":96,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Pediatric Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease","condition":"GERD","presentation":"Recurrent emesis and severe acid regurgitation since birth with sleep disturbance, while taking lansoprazole (Prevacid 15 mg).","sections":[{"name":"Quercetin titration protocol","items":[{"agent":"Weeks 1–2","dose":"Quercetin powder, 1 rounded ¼ tsp BID"},{"agent":"Weeks 3–4","dose":"Advance to ¼ tsp TID"},{"agent":"Week 5 onward","dose":"Advance to ⅓ tsp TID","why":"Blended into mashed yams, sweet potatoes, applesauce or oatmeal."},{"agent":"Mechanical / positional management","why":"Elevate the head of the crib or bed at a 30-degree incline; cease all feedings immediately before bedtime."},{"agent":"Weaning schedule","why":"Taper Prevacid to 10 mg QD after clinical stability, under physician guidance."},{"agent":"Adult reference dose","dose":"Quercetin 800 mg TID"}]}],"patient":"21-month-old male"},{"id":"case97","n":97,"chapter":"Gastroenterology","title":"Giardiasis (Giardia lamblia)","condition":"Parasites, intestinal","presentation":"Acute profuse diarrhea, malodorous flatulence and severe abdominal cramping after waterborne exposure.","sections":[{"name":"Antiprotozoal protocol","items":[{"agent":"Botanical extract compound","dose":"60 drops TID for 7 consecutive days","why":"Equal parts Hydrastis canadensis and Artemisia annua."},{"agent":"Robert's Formula","dose":"3 capsules BID for 7 days","why":"Hydrastis canadensis, Phytolacca decandra, Althaea officinalis, Echinacea angustifolia and Geranium maculatum."},{"agent":"Probiotics","dose":"At bedtime","why":"High-dose Lactobacillus acidophilus and Bifidobacterium capsules."},{"agent":"Mucosal recovery additions","why":"Quercetin and DGL powder as gut emollients, with rigorous electrolyte and water replenishment."}]}],"patient":"13-year-old female"}]};
